\v 10 Then¦316172 Yehudah's¦316175 officials¦316174 heard¦316172 \add ≈about what was going on\add*, and¦316172 they went¦316179 up¦316179 from¦316180 the \add ≈palace\add* to \add ≈the temple where\add* they sat in the gateway at the New Gate at Yahweh's¦316184 \add ≈residence\add*.
\v 11 Then the priests¦316194 and the prophets¦316195 spoke to the officials¦316198 and to all the people¦316203, saying¦316193, “It's right for this man¦316208 to die, because¦316210 he¦316211 prophesied¦316211 against¦316212 this city¦316214, as¦316216 you've all heard¦316217 with¦316218 your¦316218 own¦316218 ears¦316218.”
\p
\v 12 \add ≈So¦316220\add* Yirmeyah¦316221 spoke to all the officials¦316226 and all the people¦316231 and said¦316220, “Yahweh¦316233 has sent¦316234 me out to prophesy¦316235 to say¦316232 all the words¦316247 that¦316248 you have¦316249 heard¦316249, against¦316236 \add both\add* this \add ≈temple\add* and this city¦316242.
\v 13 \add ≈So¦316251 now¦316251,\add* improve your ways¦316253 and your \add ≈practices\add*, and listen¦316255 to¦316256 the voice¦316256 of your god¦316258 Yahweh¦316257 so¦316259 that he'll¦316259 relent concerning¦316261 the disaster that he's¦316265 proclaimed against you all.
\v 14 \add ≈As for me,\add* here¦316269 I am¦316270 in¦316270 your \add #hands\add*—do¦316271 to¦316273 me \add ≈whatever you think\add* is right¦316275 and¦316268 proper.
\v 15 \add ≈However,\add* you must¦316281 surely know that¦316298 if you kill me, then you're all bringing innocent¦316291 blood¦316290 on yourselves¦316294 and on this¦316298 city¦316297 and its¦316301 inhabitants¦316301, because¦316282 Yahweh¦316305 has¦316304 truly sent¦316304 me to you to proclaim all these¦316313 messages¦316312 for you all \add ≈to hear\add*.”
