\v 17 Then¦316341 \add ≈some\add* of \add Yehudah's\add* elders¦316343 \add ≈stepped forward\add* and¦316341 spoke to¦316346 all¦316348 the people¦316351 who were gathered there,
\v 18 “Micah (\add Heb. Mikah,\add* the Morashtite) prophesied¦316358 \add ≈during the lifetime\add* of¦316382 Yehudah's¦316363 King¦316361 Hizkiyah\add !(Hezekiah)\add*, and¦316364 he¦316364 told all¦316367 the people¦316369 from Yehudah that Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦316376 says¦316374 this:
\q1 Tsiyyon¦316378 \add !(Zion¦316378)\add*, a field¦316379 will¦316380 be¦316380 ploughed,
\q1 and Yerushalem¦316381 will become heaps¦316382 \add of ruins\add*,
\q1 and the¦316369 \add ≈temple\add* hill¦316384 will become an \add ≈overgrown\add* forest¦316387.\x + \xo 26:18: \xt Mic 3:12.\x*
\m
\v 19 Did¦316390 Yehudah's¦316394 King¦316392 Hizkiyah or anyone else in Yehudah put¦316390 him¦316390 to death¦316390? Didn't \add @Hizkiyah\add* \add ≈respect and honour\add* Yahweh and \add ≈ask for\add* \add *his\add* favour, and didn't¦316398 Yahweh \add ≈relent from sending\add* the¦316412 disaster that he¦316415 had¦316415 pronounced against them¦316416? \add ≈It¦316408 seems that\add* we're¦316417 about¦316418 to bring great¦316420 \add ≈harm\add* on¦316421 ourselves.”
\p
\v 20 \add ≈Now\add* there was¦316428 \add ≈another\add* man¦316427 prophesying¦316429 in¦316430 Yahweh's¦316431 name¦316430 of Yahweh: Uriyah¦316432 (son¦316433 of Shemayah¦316435 from¦316436 Kiriat¦316436-Yearim) who prophesied¦316438 against this city¦316441 and¦316425 against this land¦316445 \add ≈with similar\add* messages¦316448 to Yirmeyah¦316449.
