\v 23 They¦316490 brought¦316490 Uriyah¦316493 back from¦316494 Egypt¦316494 and took¦316495 him to¦316496 King¦316498 Yehoyakim¦316499 \add ≈who ran him through with¦316501 a sword¦316501\add* and threw¦316502 his¦316505 corpse¦316505 into the \add ≈public graveyard¦316508\add*.
\p
\v 24 However, Shafan's¦316517 son¦316515 Ahikam¦316514 \add ≈supported\add* Yirmeyah¦316521 and \add ≈didn't¦316522 allow the people¦316528 to kill him¦316529\add*.
\c 27
