\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 At the beginning¦316532 of the reign¦316533 of Yehudah's¦316539 King¦316538 Yehoyakim¦316534 (\add Jehoiakim\add*, son¦316535 of Yoshiyah¦316537 \add Josiah\add*), this¦316542 message¦316541 came¦316540 to¦316543 Yirmeyah¦316545 \add !(Jeremiah¦316545)\add* from¦316546 Yahweh¦316547,\x + \xo 27:1: \xt 2Ki 24:18-20; 2Ch 36:11-13.\x*
\v 2 telling \add %him\add* this:
\m Make¦316553 yourself¦316556 a wooden \add ox\add* yoke with bars, and \add ≈tie\add* it to your¦316562 neck¦316562.
\v 3 \add ≈Use it to send¦316564 messages\add* to the kings of Edom¦316568, Moab¦316572, Ammon¦316577, Tsor \add !(Tyre¦316581)\add*, and¦316564 Tsidon¦316585 \add !(Sidon¦316585)\add*, \add ≈through the ambassadors\add* \add from those countries\add* who've come to Yerushalem¦316589 to \add meet with\add* King¦316567 Tsidkiyah \add !(Zedekiah¦316592)\add*
\v 4 to tell them that Yisrael's¦316608 god¦316607, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦316605 says¦316604 to give their¦316600 masters this message:
\v 5 I myself made¦316616 the earth \add and\add* the \add #people\add* and \add #animals\add* that¦316626 are¦316627 on¦316627 the earth, by¦316631 my \add ≈direct actions\add* and my great¦316632 strength, and I give¦316635 it¦316635 to¦316636 whoever I \add ≈see fit\add*.
\v 6 Now¦316640 I've \add ≈personally handed over\add* all¦316645 these¦316648 lands¦316647 to my servant¦316654, the Babylonian King¦316651 Nebuchadnezzar¦316650, and¦316640 I've also given the animals¦316658 in the countryside¦316659 to him to serve¦316662 him.
\v 7 All the nations will serve him and his son¦316671 and then his \add ≈grandson\add*, until¦316677 the time¦316680 of his own land¦316681 comes¦316678 \add due\add*. \add ≈Yes, it will\add*, and then many nations and great¦316690 kings¦316689 will make him serve them.
\p
\v 8 Any nation or kingdom¦316694 that won't serve¦316698 the Babylonian King Nebuchadnezzar and that won't put¦316710 its¦316713 neck¦316713 into his yoke¦316714, then¦316692 I'll¦316720 punish that nation with¦316717 \add ≈war\add* and famine¦316718 and \add ≈disease\add* until¦316728 I've¦316730 used \add @King Nebuchadnezzar\add* to finish them \add off\add*. That is Yahweh's¦316727 declaration,
\v 9 \add ≈so\add* don't¦316735 you all keep listening¦316737 to your ‘prophets¦316740’, and to your diviners¦316743 and dreamers¦316745, and to your soothsayers¦316748 and sorcerers¦316751—all those who¦316752 keep telling you that you all won't¦316735 serve¦316759 the¦316762 Babylonian¦316763 king¦316762,
\v 10 because¦316765 they're¦316767 prophesying¦316768 lies to you, so¦316770 as¦316770 to remove¦316771 you all far¦316771 away¦316771 from¦316773 on your land. \add ≈Yes,\add* I¦316775 will¦316775 drive¦316775 you all out¦316775 and¦316777 you'll die \add in a foreign land\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈However,\add* the nation that brings¦316781 its neck¦316784 into the Babylonian king's yoke and serves¦316789 him¦316789, I'll¦316790 let¦316790 \add @that nation\add* remain¦316790 on¦316791 its land¦316793, and it will¦316798 cultivate it and live \add ≈there\add*. That's is Yahweh's¦316796 declaration.
\p
\v 12 Then¦316801 to Yehudah's¦316806 King¦316804 Tsidkiyah \add !(Zedekiah¦316803)\add*, I¦316807 \add ≈passed on\add* those \add same\add* words¦316810, saying¦316812, “Put your necks¦316816 into the yoke¦316817 of the Babylonian king¦316818, and serve¦316821 him¦316822 and his¦316823 people¦316823, and live¦316824.
\v 13 Why would you¦316828 and your¦316829 people¦316829 die¦316827 from \add ≈war\add*, famine¦316831, and \add ≈disease\add*, as¦316833 Yahweh¦316835 has¦316834 \add ≈said will come to any\add* nation¦316838 that¦316839 doesn't serve¦316842 the Babylonian king¦316845?
\v 14 \add ≈So¦316848\add* don't¦316848 listen¦316850 to the messages¦316853 from the prophets¦316854 who¦316855 are¦316855 speaking to you when they tell¦316855 you all not to serve¦316859 the king¦316862 of¦316862 Babylon¦316863 as they're¦316866 prophesying¦316867 lies to you
\v 15 because¦316870 I didn't¦316871 send¦316872 them¦316872. Yahweh¦316875 declares that they're¦316876 using my¦316878 name¦316878 to prophesy¦316877 lies so¦316880 that I'll drive¦316881 you out¦316881, and you'll all perish¦316883—\add both\add* you and the¦316885 prophets¦316885 who¦316886 are¦316886 prophesying¦316886 to you.”
\v 16 Then¦316889 I¦316898 told the priests¦316891 and all¦316894 those people¦316896 that Yahweh says¦316901: Don't¦316903 listen¦316905 to the words¦316908 of your prophets¦316909 who¦316910 are¦316910 prophesying to you and saying that the utensils from Yahweh's¦316902 \add ≈temple\add* will¦316910 \add ≈soon\add* be¦316918 brought¦316918 back¦316918 from Babylon¦316919, because¦316922 they're¦316924 prophesying lies to you.
\v 17 Don't¦316928 listen¦316930 to¦316931 them¦316931. Serve¦316932 the Babylonian king¦316935 and¦316938 live¦316938. Why should this¦316942 city¦316941 become¦316940 a ruin¦316943?
\v 18 If they¦316948 were prophets¦316947 \add ≈who really have access to\add* Yahweh's message¦316952, then¦316945 please¦316958 let¦316956 them¦316956 intercede with Commander-in-chief Yahweh so that¦316966 the¦316964 utensils remaining¦316966 in Yahweh's \add ≈temple\add* and in Yehudah's¦316972 king's¦316971 \add ≈palace\add* and in Yerushalem¦316973 \add ≈don't¦316961 end up being taken\add* to Babylon¦316974.
\p
\v 19 \add ≈Yes,\add* Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦316980 has spoken about¦316982 the \add bronze\add* pillars¦316984 and the \add large, bronze\add* \add ≈water basin\add*, and concerning¦316982 the \add bronze\add* stands¦316990 and the rest of¦316992 the utensils remaining¦316992 in this¦316996 city¦316995,
\v 20 which the Babylonian King Nebuchadnezzar¦317002 didn't¦316999 take when¦317005 he¦317005 exiled¦317005 Yehudah's¦317015 King Yekonyah (\add Jeconiah,\add* son of \add Yehoyakim/\add*Jehoiakim) from¦317016 Yerushalem to¦317017 Babylon¦317004, along with all¦317019 the nobles¦317021 of Yehudah including¦317018 Yerushalem.
\v 21 Yisrael's¦317032 god¦317031, Commander-in-chief Yahweh says¦317028 about the utensils remaining¦317036 in Yahweh's¦317029 \add ≈temple\add* and in the \add ≈palace\add* of the king¦317040 of Yehudah¦317042 and Yerushalem¦317043:
\v 22 They'll be¦317046 taken¦317046 to Babylon and they'll¦317046 remain¦317048 there¦317047 until¦317049 the \add ≈time when I punish\add* \add @those Babylonians\add*, and then I'll¦317056 bring¦317056 them \add ≈back\add* and restore them to this¦317061 place¦317060. That is Yahweh's¦317055 declaration.
\c 28
\s1 Yirmeyah vs Prophet Hananyah
\rem /s1 Jeremiah Condemns Hananiah; The False Prophet Hananiah; Jeremiah and the Prophet Hananiah; Hananiah Opposes Jeremiah and Dies
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 In the fifth¦317078 month¦317077 of the fourth¦317076 year of the reign¦317069 of Yehudah's¦317073 King¦317071 Tsidkiyah \add !(Zedekiah¦317070)\add*, Azzur's¦317084 son¦317082 Hananyah¦317081 who¦317086 was¦317087 a ‘prophet¦317085’ from¦317087 Gibeon¦317087, said¦317079 to me in Yahweh's¦317089 \add ≈temple\add* as priests¦317091 and¦317092 all¦317092 the people¦317094 \add watched\add*, saying¦317079,\x + \xo 28:1: \xt 2Ki 24:18-20; 2Ch 36:11-13.\x*
\v 2 “Yisrael's¦317103 god¦317102, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317100 says¦317099: I've broken¦317105 the yoke¦317108 of the Babylonian king¦317109.
\v 3 Within two¦317114 years¦317114, I¦317116, myself, will¦317117 bring¦317117 back¦317117 here all¦317124 the utensils from Yahweh's¦317128 residence that¦317129 the Babylonian King¦317133 Nebuchadnezzar¦317131 got from this place and¦317140 took¦317130 to Babylon¦317135.
\v 4 I, myself, will \add ≈also\add* bring¦317161 Yekonyah (\add Jeconiah,\add* the son¦317146 of Yehudah's¦317151 King¦317149 Yehoyakim¦317148/\add Jehoiakim\add*) back¦317161 to this¦317165 place¦317164, and¦317143 all¦317154 the exiles¦317156 from Yehudah that¦317165 were taken to Babylon¦317159, because¦317169 I'll¦317160 break¦317170 the yoke¦317173 of the Babylonian king¦317174. That is Yahweh's¦317168 declaration.”
\p
\v 5 Then¦317177 the prophet Yirmeyah¦317178 spoke to¦317180 the prophet Hananyah¦317182, as the priests¦317185 and¦317186 all¦317187 the people¦317189 standing¦317190 in¦317191 Yahweh's¦317192 \add ≈temple\add* \add ≈watched\add*,
\v 6 saying¦317194, “Let it¦317194 be so—may¦317199 Yahweh do¦317199 all that. May¦317201 Yahweh \add ≈confirm\add* your¦317205 messages¦317205 that you¦317207 prophesied¦317196, to bring¦317208 the \add ≈temple utensils\add* back¦317208 to this place¦317219, along with all the exiles¦317215 from¦317216 Babylon¦317216.
\v 7 However, please¦317226 listen to¦317224 this¦317228 message¦317227 that¦317229 I¦317230, myself, am¦317231 speaking¦317231 \add ≈as you and¦317233 all¦317234 the¦317236 people¦317236 listen\add*:
\v 8 The prophets¦317238 who \add ≈preceded\add* \add both\add* me and you¦317242, prophesied¦317246 \add ≈long ago\add* that many¦317250 \add ≈nations\add* and powerful kingdoms¦317253 would experience wars, \add ≈terrible suffering\add*, and \add ≈deadly diseases\add*.
\v 9 The prophet who¦317260 prophesies¦317261 about peace¦317262, \add &that\add* prophet will¦317266 be¦317266 known as ‘a truthful¦317272 prophet sent¦317270 by Yahweh¦317271’ \add only\add* when his message¦317264 comes¦317263 \add to pass\add*.”
\p
\v 10 Then¦317274 the prophet Hananyah¦317275 took¦317274 the yoke bar off the prophet Yirmeyah's¦317282 neck, and¦317274 broke¦317284 it¦317284.
\v 11 Then as all the people¦317291 watched, he¦317294 said¦317286, “This is what Yahweh¦317295 says¦317294: Just like that, I'll¦317297 break¦317297 the yoke¦317300 of the Babylonian King¦317303 Nebuchadnezzar¦317302 off the neck¦317311 of all the nations¦317314 within two¦317307 more years¦317307.”
\p Then the prophet¦317317 Yirmeyah¦317316 \add ≈left the gathering\add*.
\p
\v 12 ⇔After the prophet Hananyah¦317330 broke¦317329 the yoke bar that had been on the prophet Yirmeyah's¦317327 neck, Yahweh's¦317324 message¦317322 came to¦317325 Yirmeyah saying¦317339,
\v 13 “Go and tell Hananyah¦317345 this: ‘Yahweh¦317349 says¦317348 that you've¦317352 broken¦317352 wooden yoke bars, but¦317342 in¦317354 their¦317354 place¦317354, you'll¦317342 make¦317353 yoke bars out of iron¦317356,’
\v 14 because¦317358 Yisrael's¦317365 god¦317364, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317362 says¦317361, ‘I've put¦317368 an iron yoke bar on¦317369 the neck¦317371 of¦317371 all¦317373 these¦317376 nations¦317375 to¦317377 serve the Babylonian King¦317381 Nebuchadnezzar¦317380, and¦317384 they¦317384 will¦317384 \add indeed\add* serve him. I've also¦317385 given¦317390 him the animals¦317388 from the countryside¦317389.’ ”
\p
\v 15 Then¦317393 the prophet Yirmeyah¦317394 told the prophet Hananyah, “Listen¦317400, please¦317402, Hananyah. Yahweh¦317407 hasn't sent¦317406 you, and¦317393 you yourself have¦317409 made¦317409 this¦317413 people¦317412 \add group\add* \add ≈put their trust in things that¦317413 aren't¦317404 true\add*.
\v 16 Because¦317430 of¦317423 that, Yahweh says¦317420 this: ‘Listen, I'm¦317422 \add ≈removing you from¦317424 this world\add*. \add ≈You'll die¦317429 this very\add* year¦317427, because¦317430 you have¦317433 \add ≈said things that would cause the people to rebel¦317432\add* against¦317434 Yahweh.’ ”
\p
\v 17 The¦317440 prophet¦317440 Hananyah¦317439 then¦317438 died¦317438 in¦317441 the¦317442 seventh¦317444 month¦317443 of that¦317442 year¦317441.
\c 29
\s1 Yirmeyah's letter to the exiled Jews
\rem /s1 Jeremiah's Letter to the Exiles in Babylon; Jeremiah's Letter to the Jews in Babylonia
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 The prophet¦317453 Yirmeyah¦317452 sent¦317451 a \add ≈letter¦317449\add* from Yerushalem to the remainder¦317457 of the elders¦317458 of the exile¦317472, and to the priests¦317462, and to the prophets¦317465, and to all¦317468 the people¦317470 that¦317450 Nebuchadnezzar¦317473 had¦317472 exiled¦317472 from Yerushalem to Babylon¦317475\x + \xo 29:1-2: \xt 2Ki 24:12-16; 2Ch 36:10.\x*
\v 2 after the \add ≈removal\add* from Yerushalem of King¦317481 Yekonyah \add !(Jeconiah¦317479)\add* and the queen¦317482 mother, the \add ≈court¦317483 officials¦317484\add* and the leaders of Yehudah¦317485 and Yerushalem, plus¦317482 the craftsmen¦317487 and the metalsmiths.
\v 3 \add He sent it\add* with Shafan's¦317495 son Elasah¦317492 and¦317496 Hilkiyah's¦317499 son Gemaryah¦317496, who Yehudah's¦317505 King Tsidkiyah \add !(Zedekiah¦317502)\add* sent to the Babylonian King Nebuchadnezzar¦317508 in Babylon¦317510. \add The letter\add* said¦317512,
\pi1
\v 4 Yisrael's¦317520 god¦317519, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317517 says¦317516 this to all¦317521 \add ≈of you\add* that I've¦317526 exiled¦317523 from¦317527 Yerushalem¦317527 to Babylon¦317528:
\v 5 Build¦317530 houses¦317531 and live in them, and plant¦317533 gardens¦317534 and eat¦317535 their¦317538 fruit.
\v 6 \add ≈Marry\add* and \add ≈have children\add*. \add ≈Find\add* wives¦317547 for¦317546 your sons¦317546 and give¦317551 your daughters¦317550 \add ≈in marriage\add* so¦317553 that¦317553 they¦317553 \add also\add* \add ≈have children\add*. \add ≈Increase¦317556 in number\add* there¦317558—don't¦317559 become fewer.
\v 7 \add ≈In addition¦317563, the city¦317567 that I've¦317569 sent¦317569 you all into¦317569 exile¦317569 to, work to make it more prosperous\add* and¦317563 pray¦317572 to Yahweh¦317576 for it, because¦317577 \add ≈if¦317577 it prospers, its¦317578 prosperity will¦317579 belong¦317579 to all of you\add*.
\v 8 That's because¦317584 Yisrael's¦317590 god¦317589, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317587 says¦317586 this: Don't¦317591 let¦317593 your prophets¦317595 and diviners¦317599 who¦317596 are¦317598 among you deceive¦317593 you, and don't¦317591 listen¦317602 to¦317603 your dreams¦317605 that¦317606 you \add wishfully\add* dream,
\v 9 because¦317610 \add @those prophets\add* are¦317613 prophesying¦317613 \add ≈using\add* my¦317615 name¦317615 \add ≈but not¦317616 being truthful\add*—I¦317617 didn't¦317616 send¦317617 them¦317617. That is Yahweh's¦317620 declaration.
\p
\v 10 “Because this is what Yahweh¦317627 says¦317626: When seventy¦317632 years \add ≈have passed\add* for¦317631 Babylon¦317631, I'll visit \add ≈take notice of¦317640 you all\add* \add again\add*, and¦317636 I'll \add ≈implement\add* my¦317640 good¦317641 message¦317640 about you—to bring¦317642 you all back¦317642 to this place¦317646,\x + \xo 29:10: \xt 2Ch 36:21; Jer 25:11; Dan 9:2.\x*
\v 11 because¦317649 I know¦317651 the¦317654 plans that¦317655 I \add ≈have\add* for you all: plans for peaceful well-being¦317663—not to bring you all harm¦317665, \add but rather\add* a future¦317668 \add ≈with\add* hope¦317669. That is Yahweh's¦317661 declaration.
\v 12 Then¦317671 you'll all call¦317671 out to me \add for help\add*, and you'll come¦317673 and pray¦317674 to me, and I'll¦317676 listen¦317676 to you all.
\v 13 You'll search¦317679 for me, and¦317681 you'll find¦317681 me, because¦317682 you'll all \add ≈want to follow me with complete sincerity\add*.\x + \xo 29:13: \xt Deu 4:29.\x*
\v 14 Then¦317688, Yahweh has declared, I'll let¦317688 myself¦317688 be¦317688 found¦317688 by you all, and I'll \add ≈bring you back from\add* captivity¦317696. I'll gather¦317698 you all from all the nations¦317702 and all the places¦317705 that I banished¦317707 you to, and I'll bring you all back to the place¦317717 that I sent¦317720 you into¦317720 exile¦317720 from. That is Yahweh's¦317692 declaration.
\pi1
\v 15 Because¦317724 you've all said¦317725 that Yahweh¦317728 has¦317726 \add ≈appointed\add* prophets¦317729 for¦317727 \add %you\add* \add there\add* in Babylon¦317730,
\v 16 \add ≈then\add* Yahweh¦317738 \add ≈has something to¦317743 say¦317737\add* about the king¦317741 sitting¦317742 on David's¦317746 throne¦317745 and¦317747 about all¦317749 the people¦317751 living in¦317753 this¦317754 city¦317753—your relatives who¦317756 didn't¦317757 go¦317759 into exile¦317761 with¦317760 you.
\v 17 So Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317765 says¦317764: Listen, I'm¦317767 about¦317768 to¦317768 send¦317768 \add ≈war\add*, famine¦317775 and \add ≈deadly diseases\add* against them. I'll¦317779 make¦317779 them like¦317781 rotten¦317782 figs¦317781 that¦317783 are so bad they're \add ≈inedible\add*.
\v 18 \add ≈Yes,\add* I'll chase after¦317790 them with \add ≈war\add*, famine¦317792, and \add ≈deadly diseases\add*, and I'll make¦317794 them become a horror to all the \add ≈world's\add* kingdoms¦317799—a curse¦317801 and a desolation, and a reproach¦317804 and \add ≈something to be hissed at\add* by all the nations¦317807 where¦317808 I've¦317810 driven them,
\v 19 because they¦317818 didn't listen to my messages¦317821 that¦317825 I¦317826 sent¦317826 to them¦317827 \add ≈over and over again\add* via my servants¦317830 the¦317831 prophets¦317831, but¦317833 all you \add exiles\add* didn't listen. That¦317838 is Yahweh's¦317824 declaration.
\p
\v 20 \add ≈But¦317840\add* all¦317845 you exiles¦317847 that I¦317850 sent¦317850 away from¦317851 Yerushalem¦317851 to Babylon¦317852, listen¦317841 to Yahweh's¦317844 message¦317842:
\pi1
\v 21 Yisrael's¦317861 god¦317860, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317858, says¦317857 this about¦317880 Kolayah's¦317867 son Ahav¦317864 and Maaseyah's¦317873 son Tsidkiyah¦317870, who¦317874 are¦317874 \add both\add* prophesying¦317874 untruths to you in my¦317876 name¦317876: Listen, I'm¦317878 \add ≈handing them over\add* to the Babylonian King¦317884 Nebuchadnezzar¦317883, and he'll¦317887 \add ≈kill them right in front of¦317888 you\add*.
\v 22 Then¦317890 because of them¦317891, a \add new\add* curse¦317892 \add phrase\add* will¦317890 be¦317890 taken¦317890 on by all¦317893 the \add ≈Jewish\add* exiles¦317894 in Babylon¦317897, which goes, “May¦317899 Yahweh¦317900 make¦317899 you¦317899 like Tsidkiyah¦317901 and¦317902 Ahav¦317902, who were roasted¦317905 in the fire¦317909 by the Babylonian king¦317906,”
\v 23 because they did¦317913 something shameful in Yisrael¦317915 and they have committed¦317916 adultery¦317916 with the wives¦317919 of their neighbours¦317920, and they spoke¦317921 untrue messages¦317922 in my¦317923 name¦317923 that I hadn't commanded¦317927 them¦317927 to. I am the one \add ≈who knows that\add* and I'm a witness¦317933. That is Yahweh's¦317936 declaration.
\s1 Message to false prophet Shemayah
\rem /s1 A Message for Shemaiah; Message to Shemaiah; The Letter of Shemaiah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 24 \add Yahweh told me to\add* tell Shemayah¦317941 (the¦317942 Nehelamite¦317942) this:
\v 25 Yisrael's¦317952 god¦317951, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317949 says¦317948 this: Because¦317954 you sent¦317957 letters¦317959 in your¦317958 name¦317958 to all the people¦317964 in Yerushalem¦317966, and to the priest¦317973 Tsefanyah (Maaseyah's¦317972 son¦317970), and to all the priests¦317977, to tell \add <Tsefanyah\add*:
\pi1
\v 26 Yahweh has¦317981 made¦317981 you, \add Tsefanyah,\add* priest in place¦317983 of¦317983 the priest Yehoyada¦317984 \add !(Jehoiada¦317984)\add*, to¦317986 be¦317986 \add #overseer¦317987\add* in Yahweh's¦317980 \add ≈temple\add* over every¦317990 man who raves \add out loud\add*, making himself a prophet¦317994, and you must¦317995 put him¦317996 in the stocks¦317999 \add ≈with an iron¦318002 collar¦318002 around his\add* neck.
\v 27 \add ≈So¦318004 why\add* haven't you rebuked¦318007 Yirmeyah¦318008 the¦318009 Antotite¦318009 who's¦318010 prophesying¦318010 to¦318011 you all,
\v 28 because¦318013 he's¦318017 sent¦318017 \add a letter\add* to¦318018 us¦318018 \add here\add* in Babylon¦318019 saying¦318020, “\add @Your exile\add* \add ≈will¦318021 last a long¦318021 time\add*. Build¦318023 houses¦318024 and live in them. Plant¦318026 gardens¦318027 and eat¦318028 their¦318031 fruit.”
\p
\v 29 The priest¦318035 Tsefanyah¦318034 read that¦318039 letter¦318038 to the prophet¦318042 Yirmeyah¦318041,
\v 30 then Yahweh¦318048 \add ≈gave\add* this message¦318046 to Yirmeyah¦318051:
\v 31 Send to all the \add #exiles¦318059\add* to tell them: This is what Yahweh¦318063 says¦318062 about¦318064 Shemayah the Nehelamite¦318067: Because¦318068 Shemayah has¦318070 prophesied¦318070 to you all, \add ≈even though\add* I¦318073 didn't¦318074 send¦318075 him¦318075, and he made¦318076 you trust \add ≈what's not true\add*,
\v 32 therefore Yahweh says¦318085 this: Listen, I \add ≈will punish\add* Shemayah¦318091 the Nehelamite¦318092 and \add ≈his descendants\add*. \add ≈None of his family\add* will live among this people, and \add ≈he won't¦318096 experience the good¦318111 things\add* that¦318112 I'll¦318114 do¦318115 for¦318117 my people, because¦318121 he's¦318124 \add ≈encouraged\add* rebellion¦318123 against Yahweh. That is Yahweh's¦318086 declaration.
\c 30
\s1 Yahweh's promises to his people
\rem /s1 The Lord's Promises to His People; Restoration of Israel; Promises of Deliverance; Promises of restoration for the people; Restoration Promised for Israel and Judah
\s4 Both kingdoms
\p
\v 1 Yahweh¦318137 \add ≈gave\add* Yirmeyah¦318135 a message¦318130, saying¦318138:
\v 2 Yisrael's¦318145 god¦318144, Yahweh¦318143 says¦318142 this: Write¦318147 down on a scroll all¦318151 the¦318153 messages¦318153 that¦318154 I've¦318156 \add ≈given\add* you¦318157,
\v 3 because¦318162 listen to Yahweh's¦318168 declaration: The \add ≈time¦318164\add* is coming¦318165 when I'll restore my people¦318173 of Yisrael¦318174 and Yehudah¦318175 from captivity¦318172, and I'll bring¦318178 them¦318178 back¦318178 to the¦318181 land¦318181 that¦318182 I have to their¦318185 ancestors¦318185, and they'll¦318186 \add ≈take¦318186 possession¦318186 of it¦318186\add* \add again\add*.
\p
\v 4 \add ≈Now\add* these¦318189 are¦318190 the¦318190 messages¦318190 that¦318191 Yahweh¦318193 spoke¦318192 concerning¦318194 Yisrael¦318196 and¦318197 Yehudah¦318199:
\q1
\v 5 \add ≈Yes,\add* Yahweh¦318205 says¦318204 this:
\q1 A \add ≈cry of¦318206 panic and terror\add* has¦318208 been heard¦318208,
\q1 ≈and there's¦318210 no peace¦318211.
\q1
\v 6 Please¦318215 ask and¦318216 \add ≈find out\add*: can \add #males\add* give birth¦318219?
\q1 Why¦318221 do I¦318222 see¦318216 every¦318223 strong man¦318225 with his hands¦318226 on¦318227 his \add ≈hips\add* like¦318230 a woman \add ≈in labour\add*?
\q1 And¦318231 \add ≡why¦318221 has\add* \add ≈everyone's faces¦318234 gone so pale\add*?
\q1
\v 7 Oh dear, \add ≈that will¦318239 be¦318239 a terrible day¦318240 like¦318243 nothing that's come before\add*.
\q1 ≈It'll be a distressing¦318246 time¦318244 for¦318248 Yakov¦318248 \add !(Jacob¦318248)\add*,
\q1 →\add ≈but\add* he'll¦318250 be rescued from¦318249 it¦318249.
\p
\v 8 Then¦318252 Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦318257 declares that \add ≈at that time\add* I'll break¦318259 his¦318260 yoke¦318260 off your neck¦318262, and I'll \add ≈pull\add* your \add ≈chains\add* apart¦318264, and foreigners will¦318267 no longer enslave \add @your country\add*.
\v 9 Then¦318273 they'll¦318273 serve¦318273 their god¦318276 Yahweh¦318275, and¦318273 their king¦318279 \add on David's throne\add* who I'll¦318281 appoint for¦318282 them¦318282.
\p
\v 10 Then Yahweh¦318293 declares:
\q1 Then you¦318300, my servant¦318289 Yakov¦318290 \add !(Jacob¦318290)\add*, don't be¦318296 afraid,
\q1 ≈and¦318302 don't be dismayed¦318296, Yisrael¦318297 \add !(Israel¦318297)\add*,
\q1 because¦318298 listen, I'm¦318299 rescuing you from¦318301 afar,
\q1 and your offspring from the¦318305 land¦318305 \add ≈where they were held captive¦318306\add*.
\q1 \add ≈Yisrael\add* will¦318307 return¦318307 and be left alone and at¦318310 ease¦318310,
\q1 and there¦318311 won't¦318286 be anyone¦318312 making it afraid.\x + \xo 30:10-11: \xt Jer 46:27-28.\x*
\q1
\v 11 Yahweh¦318320 declares:
\q1 \add ≈Yes,\add* I'm with¦318316 you to¦318321 rescue you,
\q1 because¦318322 I'll \add ≈completely¦318324 destroy\add* all¦318325 the¦318327 nations¦318327 that I've¦318330 scattered¦318330 you¦318316 to,
\q1 but I won't \add ≈completely destroy\add* you.
\q1 I'll discipline¦318338 you according to justice¦318339,
\q1 \add ≈but I won't just let you off what you deserve\add*.
\p
\v 12 \add ≈Yes,\add* Yahweh¦318348 says¦318347 this:
\q1 Your¦318350 fracture¦318350 is¦318351 incurable¦318349.
\q1 ≈Your wound¦318352 is severe¦318351.
\q1
\v 13 There's no one¦318356 pleading¦318356 your cause¦318357.
\q1 There's no medicines¦318359 for your wound.
\q1 ≈There's no healing¦318360 for you.
\q1
\v 14 All your¦318366 lovers¦318366 have forgotten¦318367 you—
\q1 ≈they don't¦318369 care¦318370 about you.
\q1 \add ≈Yes,\add* I've¦318374 struck¦318374 you \add ≈like an enemy¦318373 would\add*,
\q1 ≈with the¦318375 discipline of¦318375 a cruel¦318376 \add >person\add*,
\q1 due to the \add ≈severity of your wickedness\add*.
\q1 ≈You've \add ≈disobeyed so frequently\add*.
\q1
\v 15 Why do¦318385 you¦318385 cry¦318385 out¦318385 about your¦318388 fracture¦318388—
\q1 ≈about your incurable¦318389 pain¦318390?
\q1 Your¦318396 \add ≈wickedness has¦318397 been severe\add*.
\q1 ≈You've \add ≈disobeyed so often\add*
\q1 →\add so\add* I've¦318397 done¦318397 those things to¦318399 you.
\q1
\v 16 \add ≈Because of that\add*, all¦318406 those¦318404 who¦318404 devoured you¦318404 will¦318405 be¦318405 devoured,
\q1 ≈and¦318406 all of your¦318408 adversaries, every one of them¦318409, will go¦318411 into captivity¦318410.
\q1 Then the ones plundering¦318413 you will become like plunder¦318414,
\q1 ≈and all those preying on you, I'll¦318418 give \add >to you\add* as spoil¦318419.
\q1
\v 17 \add ≈Yes,\add* I'll bring¦318422 healing¦318423 to¦318424 you¦318426,
\q1 and¦318425 I'll heal¦318426 you from¦318425 your¦318425 wounds¦318425
\q1 because¦318430 they've called¦318432 you an outcast.
\q1 ‘She is¦318434 Tsiyyon¦318434 \add !(Zion)\add*—no one¦318436 cares¦318436 about her.’
\q1 That is Yahweh's¦318429 declaration.
\p
\v 18 Yahweh¦318444 says¦318443 this:
\q1 Listen, I'm¦318445 restoring the¦318448 fortune of¦318448 Yakov's¦318450 \add !(Jacob's¦318450)\add* \add ≈descendants\add*,
