\v 21 I'll¦321268 \add ≈hand\add* Yehudah's¦321264 King¦321262 Tsidkiyah \add !(Zedekiah¦321261)\add* and his¦321267 leaders \add ≈over\add* to their enemies¦321270 and to those¦321272 who \add ≈want to see them dead\add*, and to the army¦321275 of the Babylonian king¦321276 who's \add ≈attacking\add* you.
\v 22 This is Yahweh's¦321285 declaration: Listen, I'm¦321281 about¦321282 to order them¦321286 back¦321286 to battle against this¦321290 city¦321289, and they'll¦321291 capture¦321293 it and \add ≈set it on fire¦321295\add*. Then I'll¦321286 make¦321300 Yehudah's¦321299 \add other\add* cities¦321298 into \add ≈deserted\add* wastelands¦321301.
\c 35
\s1 Praising the faithful Rekavites
\rem /s1 The Recabites; The Rechabites Commended; Jeremiah and the Rechabites; The Faithful Recabites
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add Several years earlier,\add* when Yehoyakim¦321316 \add !(Jehoiakim¦321316)\add* son¦321317 of Yoshiyah¦321319 \add !(Josiah¦321319)\add* was the king¦321320 of Yehudah¦321321 \add !(Judah¦321321)\add*, Yahweh¦321314 \add ≈had given\add* Yirmeyah¦321312 \add !(Jeremiah¦321312)\add* this message¦321306:\x + \xo 35:1: \xt 2Ki 23:36–24:6; 2Ch 36:5-7.\x*
\v 2 Go to the Rekavite clan and talk with them, then bring¦321331 them into one¦321336 of¦321337 the rooms¦321337 in my \add ≈temple\add*, and give¦321338 them wine¦321340 to drink¦321338.
\v 3 \add ≈So¦321342\add* I took¦321342 Yaazanyah¦321345 (son of Yirmeyah¦321348, son of Havatsinyah) and his brothers¦321354 and his sons, and all¦321361 the \add rest of\add* the Rekavite clan,
\v 4 and¦321366 I took them¦321367 to¦321370 the rooms of the sons¦321373 of Hanan¦321374 (son of Igdalyah¦321377, man¦321378 of God) at the \add ≈temple\add*. Those rooms were beside¦321382 the leaders' room, which¦321385 was¦321386 above¦321386 the room of Maaseyah¦321388 (Shallum's¦321391 son), the gatekeeper.
\v 5 Then¦321395 I¦321406 placed bowls¦321402 and cups¦321405 of wine¦321410 in¦321396 front¦321396 of the Rekavites¦321401 and told them to drink¦321408 some.
\p
\v 6 \add ≈But¦321412\add* they¦321412 \add ≈responded¦321412\add*, “We¦321414 don't¦321413 drink wine, because¦321417 our ancestor¦321422, Rekav's¦321421 son¦321419 Yonadav¦321418, commanded¦321423 \add all of\add* us and¦321412 our descendants not to ever drink any wine.
\v 7 \add ≡He also told us\add* not to build¦321439 any houses¦321436, \add ≈or to plant¦321447 any crops\add* or vineyards¦321444, \add saying\add* that \add %we\add* must¦321449 \add ≈always\add* live¦321458 in tents¦321452, so¦321457 that \add %we'd\add* \add ≈have long lives in the land that we're staying in\add* \add as foreigners\add*.
\v 8 We've \add ≈obeyed\add* the voice¦321471 of our ancestor¦321476, Rekav's¦321475 son¦321473 Yonadav¦321472 in everything that¦321478 he¦321479 commanded¦321479 us¦321479 \add and\add* we¦321487, our wives¦321488, and our children \add ≈have¦321470 never drunk¦321481 wine¦321483 in our lives\add*.
\v 9 We'll never build¦321493 houses¦321494 to live in¦321495, or \add ≈own any\add* \add #vineyards¦321496, fields¦321497\add*, or seed¦321498.
\v 10 We've lived in¦321505 tents¦321505, and¦321504 we've¦321504 \add ≈followed everything\add* that¦321509 our¦321513 ancestor¦321513 Yonadav¦321512 \add ≈told¦321511\add* us¦321511,
\v 11 \add ≈but¦321515\add* when¦321516 the Babylonian King¦321518 Nebuchadnezzar¦321517 attacked the land¦321523, we \add ≈decided that\add* we must \add ≈move\add* to Yerushalem to escape from the \add ≈Babylonian\add* and¦321515 Aramean armies, so now we're \add all\add* living in¦321535 Yerushalem.
\p
\v 12 Then Yahweh¦321541 \add ≈gave\add* this message¦321539 to Yirmeyah¦321544, saying¦321545 that
\v 13 Yisrael's¦321553 god¦321552, Commander-in-chief Yahweh says¦321549 to go¦321554 and \add ≈ask\add* the people in Yehudah¦321557, including¦321555 those who live in Yerushalem¦321559: Won't you¦321555 all accept¦321561 correction¦321562 and listen¦321563 to my¦321566 messages¦321566? This is Yahweh's¦321550 declaration:
\v 14 Rekav's¦321578 son¦321576 Yonadav¦321575 \add ≈told¦321581\add* his¦321584 descendants not¦321585 to drink¦321586 any wine¦321588 \add ≈and they've¦321590 followed that¦321579\add* to this very day¦321593. \add ≈In contrast,\add* I've \add ≈personally and consistently\add* spoken¦321601 to all of you \add ≈but¦321589 you haven't taken any notice of what I've said\add*.
\v 15 I \add ≈persistently\add* sent¦321609 all my¦321615 servants¦321615, the prophets¦321616, out to you all to tell each person to turn¦321622 from¦321626 their wicked \add >behaviour\add* and \add ≈start doing¦321630 good¦321628 instead\add*, and to \add ≈stop following\add* after¦321633 other¦321635 gods¦321634 and serving¦321636 them. Then¦321609 they'd live on the land that¦321641 I gave¦321643 to your ancestors¦321645 and to all of you, \add ≈however, you all won't¦321630 listen¦321652 to me or pay attention\add* to me.
\v 16 \add ≈Yes¦321661,\add* Yonadav's¦321658 descendants have¦321656 \add ≈followed the instructions¦321667\add* that¦321666 their ancestor¦321665 gave them¦321667, but¦321668 this¦321669 people¦321668, refuses to¦321672 \add ≈obey\add* me¦321672,
\v 17 \add ≈so¦321675\add* Yisrael's¦321683 god, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦321679, says¦321678 this: Listen, I'm \add ≈sending\add* all the disasters that¦321698 I pronounced for Yehudah¦321688, \add ≈including¦321689\add* everyone living in Yerushalem¦321693. \add ≡I'm sending them\add* against them because¦321701 I spoke¦321702 to them, but they wouldn't listen¦321705. I called¦321706 to them, but they wouldn't answer¦321709.
\p
\v 18 Then¦321711 Yirmeyah¦321714 told¦321740 the Rekavite clan that Yisrael's¦321721 god¦321720, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦321718 says¦321717 this: You've all listened¦321724 to the commands¦321735 of your ancestor¦321729 Yonadav¦321728 and¦321711 have kept¦321730 them all. You've obeyed everything that he¦321740 commanded¦321740 you all to do¦321736,
\v 19 so¦321744 Yisrael's¦321750 god¦321749, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦321747 says¦321746 this: There'll always be¦321753 someone descended from Rekav's¦321758 son¦321756 Yonadav¦321755 to serve me.
\c 36
\s1 Baruk reads out Yahweh's messages at the temple
\rem /s1 Jehoiakim Burns Jeremiah's Scroll; Baruch Reads the Scroll in the Temple; The Scroll Read in the Temple; Baruch Reads the Lord's Messages
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 In¦321767 the fourth¦321768 year¦321767 \add of the reign\add* Yehudah's¦321774 King¦321773 Yehoyakim¦321769 (or Jehoiakim, son¦321770 of Yoshiyah¦321772\add !/Josiah\add*), Yahweh¦321782 \add ≈gave\add* this¦321777 message¦321776 to Yirmeyah¦321780:\x + \xo 36:1: \xt 2Ki 24:1; 2Ch 36:5-7; Dan 1:1-2.\x*
\v 2 Get a scroll¦321788 for yourself¦321787 and write¦321791 all the messages¦321796 on it that¦321797 I've¦321799 told you concerning Yisrael¦321803 and Yehudah¦321806, and all the other nations¦321811. Do this for everything I have¦321799 said, \add back\add* from the \add ≈time\add* of¦321815 Yoshiyah¦321816 until \add ≈the present time\add*.
\v 3 Perhaps¦321821 Yehudah's¦321824 \add ≈people\add* will¦321822 hear¦321822 about all¦321826 the¦321828 disasters that¦321829 I intend to¦321833 bring on them and then turn¦321835 away from \add #their\add* wicked \add #ways\add*, so I can forgive¦321839 them for their wickedness and their disobedience.
\p
\v 4 Then Yirmeyah called¦321844 Neriyah's¦321851 son¦321849 Baruk, and Yirmeyah dictated all¦321857 the¦321859 messages¦321859 that¦321861 Yahweh¦321860 had¦321863 \add ≈given\add* to him¦321864, for Baruk to \add ≈record\add* on¦321865 a scroll¦321867.
\v 5 Then¦321871 Yirmeyah¦321872 \add ≈instructed¦321871\add* Baruk¦321875 saying¦321876, “I'm¦321877 restrained \add ≈from entering\add* Yahweh's¦321883 \add ≈residence\add*
\v 6 \add ≈so\add* you must go¦321885 and¦321885 read from the scroll¦321888 that you wrote¦321891 at my¦321893 dictation. On the day¦321902 of the fast, you must read Yahweh's¦321897 messages so that all the people in the \add ≈temple will hear them\add* as well as the \add people from\add* the rest of Yehudah's¦321908 cities¦321910. Proclaim these messages to them.
\v 7 Perhaps Yaweh \add ≈will take notice of¦321915\add* their \add ≈pleas for mercy\add*. Perhaps everyone¦321919 will turn¦321918 from¦321920 their wicked \add #ways\add*, since the¦321921 anger¦321925 and¦321926 fury that¦321927 Yahweh¦321917 has¦321929 proclaimed against¦321931 this¦321934 \add ≈nation\add* is¦321924 severe.
\v 8 \add ≈So¦321936\add* Neriyah's¦321940 son¦321938 Baruk¦321937 did everything that¦321942 the prophet¦321946 Yirmeyah¦321945 had¦321944 \add ≈told¦321944\add* him¦321944 to—he read Yahweh's messages¦321949 aloud at Yahweh's \add ≈temple\add*.
\p
\v 9 In¦321956 the ninth¦321966 month¦321965 of the \add ≈next\add* year¦321956, all¦321971 the people¦321973 in¦321974 Yerushalem¦321974 and¦321975 the \add ≈visitors to the city from¦321979 the rest of\add* Yehudah¦321964, announced a fast¦321968 \add ≈to honour\add* Yahweh¦321970.
\v 10 \add ≈Again\add* Baruk¦321984 read Yirmeyah's¦321989 messages¦321988 aloud at Yahweh's \add ≈temple\add*, from the room¦321992 of Gemaryah¦321993 (son¦321994 of the scribe¦321997 Shafan¦321996) in¦321998 the upper¦321999 courtyard¦321998, by the entrance¦322000 gate¦322001 to Yahweh's \add ≈residence\add*. He did this \add ≈so that all¦322007 the people¦322009 could hear it\add*.
\s1 The messages get read to the officials
\rem /s1 The Scroll Read in the Palace; The Scroll Is Read to the Officials
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 11 \add ≈When¦322011\add* Mikayah¦322012 (son of Gemaryah¦322015 son of Shafan¦322018) heard all¦322021 Yahweh's¦322024 messages¦322023 from¦322025 the¦322026 scroll¦322026,
\v 12 he¦322028 went down to to the \add ≈secretary's\add* room¦322034 in the \add ≈palace\add*, and wow, all the officials were¦322042 sitting¦322042 there¦322038: Elishama the \add ≈secretary\add*, Shemayah's¦322048 son Delayah¦322045, Akbor's¦322052 son Elnatan¦322049, Shafan's¦322056 son Gemaryah¦322053, and Hananyah's¦322060 son Tsidkiyah¦322057, \add ≈along with\add* all the \add other\add* officials.
\v 13 \add ≈When¦322065\add* Mikayah¦322067 reported to them¦322066 all¦322069 the messages¦322071 that¦322072 he'd heard¦322073 Baruk¦322075 read¦322074 aloud¦322074 \add ≈for the people¦322078 to hear\add*,
\v 14 the officials sent¦322080 Yehudi (son of Netanyah¦322092 son of Shelemyah¦322095 son of Kushi) to Baruk. Yehudi \add ≈ordered\add* Baruk, “Take the scroll in your¦322107 hand¦322107, the scroll from which¦322101 you¦322102 were reading in the hearing of the people¦322105, and come¦322108.” \add ≈So¦322080\add* Neriyah's¦322113 son Baruk took¦322109 the scroll and went¦322118 to the officials
\v 15 \add ≈where\add* they¦322121 told him to sit¦322123 down and¦322121 read it \add ≈to them\add*, \add ≈so\add* Baruk¦322128 \add ≈read out\add* \add the messages\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈When¦322146\add* they heard¦322132 \add ≈it all\add*, they \add ≈were¦322138 afraid and¦322131 decided together that they needed to report it\add* all to the king¦322149,
\v 17 and¦322156 they¦322159 asked¦322159 Baruk¦322158, “How¦322165 come you¦322166 wrote¦322166 down all¦322169 these¦322172 messages¦322171 from¦322173 Yirmeyah?”
\p
\v 18 “He¦322175 dictated them to¦322180 me¦322180,” he replied, “and¦322175 I¦322186 \add ≈just wrote¦322187 them down\add* on¦322188 the¦322190 scroll¦322190.”
\p
\v 19 Then the¦322195 officials¦322195 told Baruk¦322198, “Go¦322199 \add and\add* hide¦322200, and Yirmeyah¦322202 \add as well\add*. Don't¦322204 let¦322206 anyone¦322203 know¦322206 where¦322207 you¦322201 two are¦322208.”
\s1 King Yehoyakim burns the scroll
\rem /s1 The King Burns the Scroll; Jehoiakim Burns the Scroll
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 20 Then¦322210 they left the scroll¦322217 in the secretary Elishama's¦322220 room¦322219 and went¦322210 out to the king in the courtyard¦322214 and told¦322222 him everything \add they'd heard\add*.
\rem /s1 King Jehoiakim Burns the Scroll
\v 21 The¦322231 king sent¦322230 Yehudi to get the scroll¦322238, and he¦322239 went and got it from¦322240 the secretary Elishama's room¦322240. Then¦322230 Yehudi read¦322243 it \add ≈aloud¦322243\add* for the king and all¦322248 the officials¦322250 who¦322251 were¦322251 standing¦322251 beside him \add ≈to hear\add*.
\v 22 \add *That\add* month¦322259, the¦322255 king¦322255 was in his winter¦322258 house¦322257 and¦322261 a brazier was burning in front of him¦322264.
\v 23 \add ≈Whenever\add* Yehudi¦322270 had read¦322269 \add ≈a couple\add* of columns, the king would \add ≈slice it off\add* with a knife¦322275 and¦322267 toss it into¦322278 the fire¦322280 until¦322285 the entire¦322288 scroll¦322290 was gone,
\v 24 \add ≈but¦322299\add* neither the king¦322306 or any of his¦322309 servants¦322309 were afraid¦322300 of the messages¦322314 (and¦322299 they didn't¦322299 tear¦322302 their¦322305 clothes¦322305 \add to indicate repentance\add*—
\v 25 Elnatan¦322318, Delayah¦322319, and¦322317 Gemaryah¦322320 had¦322321 urged the king¦322322 not¦322323 to¦322324 burn¦322324 the scroll¦322327, but¦322317 he¦322329 \add ≈hadn't taken any notice of\add* them¦322330).
\v 26 Then¦322332 the king ordered¦322332 a \add ≈relative\add* Yerahme'el¦322336, Azriel's¦322345 son Serayah¦322342, and Abdeel's¦322351 son Shelemyah¦322348 to¦322352 arrest the scribe¦322356 Baruk¦322355 and the prophet¦322359 Yirmeyah¦322358, but¦322332 Yahweh¦322361 had hidden¦322360 them¦322360.
\s1 Yirmeyah rewrites the scroll
\rem /s1 Jeremiah Writes Another Scroll; Jeremiah Dictates Another; Jeremiah Rewrites the Scroll
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 27 After¦322371 the king¦322374 had burnt¦322373 the scroll¦322377 with the messages¦322380 on it that¦322381 Yirmeyah had dictated to Baruk¦322383, Yahweh¦322367 \add ≈gave this\add* message¦322365 to Yirmeyah:
\v 28 Get yourself¦322391 another¦322393 scroll and¦322394 write¦322394 down all¦322397 the messages¦322399 that were¦322402 on¦322403 the original scroll that Yehudah's¦322412 King¦322410 Yehoyakim \add !(Jehoiakim¦322409)\add* burnt¦322408.
\v 29 Then¦322414 you must¦322420 tell \add @the king\add* that Yahweh¦322423 says¦322422: You burnt¦322425 that scroll¦322428, asking why¦322431 it was written¦322432 that the Babylonian king would come and destroy¦322441 this¦322445 land¦322444 and leave it without people or animals¦322449.
\v 30 \add ≈Now\add* Yahweh¦322456 says¦322455 about King¦322460 Yehoyakim¦322459: No descendant of his will ever sit¦322467 on¦322468 David's¦322471 throne¦322470. As for¦322466 him¦322466, his corpse¦322472 will be¦322473 thrown¦322474 out¦322474 into the heat¦322475 of the day¦322476 and¦322477 the frost¦322477 at night¦322478.
\v 31 I'll punish him¦322481, his descendants, and his servants¦322487 for their¦322490 \add ≈wickedness\add*. The disasters that¦322505 I've¦322507 threatened them with, \add ≈but¦322480 which¦322505\add* they¦322510 \add ^ignored\add*, I'll \add ≈send\add* onto them and all Yerushalem's¦322496 inhabitants¦322495, and onto every¦322499 person in \add the rest of\add* Yehudah¦322500.
\p
\v 32 \add ≈So\add* Yirmeyah got another¦322517 scroll and gave¦322518 it¦322518 to¦322519 Baruk, son¦322522 of¦322522 Neriyah¦322524 the scribe¦322525. Yirmeyah \add again\add* dictated all¦322531 the messages that¦322535 had¦322536 been on the scroll burnt¦322536 by Yehudah's¦322540 King¦322538 Yehoyakim¦322537, and Baruk wrote¦322526 them¦322544 onto the scroll, \add ≈along with several\add* other similar messages.
\c 37
\s1 Yirmeyah's response to Tsidkiyah/Zedekiah
\rem /s1 Zedekiah's Request to Jeremiah; Jeremiah in Prison; Zedekiah Calls for Jeremiah; Zedekiah's Vain Hope
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add ≈By now\add* Yoshiyah's¦322556 son Tsidkiyah \add !(Zedekiah¦322553)\add* reigned¦322550 as king instead of Yehoyakim's¦322561 son Yehoyakin. The Babylonian King¦322552 Nebuchadnezzar¦322564 had made¦322563 Tsidkiyah king over the Yehudah¦322569 \add ≈region¦322568\add*.\x + \xo 37:1: \xt 2Ki 24:17; 2Ch 36:10.\x*
\v 2 \add ≈However,\add* \add @Tsidkiyah\add*, his servants¦322574, and¦322571 his people¦322575 wouldn't listen¦322572 to¦322577 Yahweh's¦322580 messages¦322579 that¦322581 he'd \add ≈given\add* via the prophet¦322585 Yirmeyah¦322584.
\p
\v 3 \add ≈Eventually,\add* King¦322588 Tsidkiyah¦322589, Shelemyah's¦322595 son Yehukal¦322592, and¦322587 Tsefanyah¦322598 son of¦322599 Maaseyah¦322601 the priest¦322602, sent¦322587 a message to the prophet¦322606 Yirmeyah¦322605 \add ≈requesting him\add*, “Pray¦322608 on our behalf to our god¦322615, Yahweh¦322614.
\v 4 \add ≈At that time,\add* Yirmeyah was \add still\add* coming¦322618 and¦322617 going¦322619 among the people¦322621, because he hadn't yet been put¦322624 in prison.
\v 5 Far'oh's¦322631 \add !(Pharaoh's¦322631)\add* army¦322630 had come¦322632 out of Egypt¦322633, and the \add ≈Babylonians\add* who¦322636 were¦322636 besieging Yerushalem heard¦322634 the \add ≈news¦322642\add* about them and \add ≈retreated from¦322644\add* Yerushalem.
\p
\v 6 Then Yahweh¦322651 \add ≈gave\add* Yirmeyah¦322654 this message¦322649 to proclaim:
\v 7 Yisrael's¦322663 god¦322662, Yahweh¦322661 told me that¦322679 you \add >people\add* should say¦322666 this to Yehudah's¦322670 king¦322669 who¦322671 sent¦322671 you all to consult¦322674 me: Listen¦322675 Far'oh's¦322678 army¦322677 which¦322679 was¦322679 coming¦322679 out¦322679 to help¦322681 you all is¦322682 about¦322682 to return¦322682 back to its¦322683 own¦322683 \add ≈country\add*, Egypt¦322684.
\v 8 Then¦322686 the \add ≈Babylonians¦322687\add* will return¦322686 and attack this city¦322691, then¦322686 they'll¦322686 capture¦322693 it and burn¦322694 it \add ≈down\add*.
\v 9 Yahweh¦322701 says¦322700 not¦322702 to¦322706 deceive¦322704 yourselves that the¦322710 Babylonians¦322710 have left, because¦322711 they¦322714 won't¦322702 leave,
\v 10 because¦322716 even if¦322717 you all¦322720 defeated¦322719 the entire¦322720 Babylonian¦322723 army¦322722 that's attacking you so that only wounded men¦322728 were left in¦322731 their tents, they¦322732 would get up and¦322733 burn¦322733 \add ≈down\add* this¦322737 city¦322736.
\s1 Yirmeyah is arrested and imprisoned
\rem /s1 Jeremiah Is Arrested and Imprisoned; Jeremiah Is Imprisoned
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 11 Then¦322740 when¦322741 the¦322742 Babylonian¦322743 army had¦322741 left Yerushalem¦322745 \add ≈to avoid\add* Far'oh's¦322748 army,
\v 12 Yirmeyah¦322752 left \add *the city\add* to go¦322754 to the Benyamin¦322756 \add ≈region¦322755\add* to \add ≈take possession of a section\add* \add of land\add* there¦322758 among \add &his\add* people¦322760.
\v 13 \add ≈As he went through\add* the Benyamin¦322766 gate¦322765, a chief guard¦322769 named Yiriyah¦322771 (son of Shelemyah¦322774, son of Hananyah¦322777) was there¦322767. He¦322778 seized the prophet¦322782 Yirmeyah¦322781 and¦322762 \add ≈claimed that\add* he was deserting to the \add ≈Babylonians\add*.
\p
\v 14 \add ≈But¦322790\add* Yirmeyah¦322791 \add ≈disputed\add*, “That's a lie¦322792—I'm¦322793 not¦322793 deserting to the \add ≈Babylonians\add*.” \add ≈However\add* Yiriyah¦322802 wouldn't listen¦322799 to him and he¦322801 \add ≈arrested\add* him and took him to the officials¦322807.
\v 15 The officials¦322810 were angry¦322809 at Yirmeyah¦322813 and they¦322814 \add had\add* him¦322817 beaten and put¦322816 in prison. (\add The place\add* had been the house¦322820 of¦322820 the scribe¦322822 Yonatan¦322821, but¦322809 it¦322825 had been converted into¦322827 \add ≈a prison\add*.)
\v 16 \add ≈So¦322843\add* Yirmeyah¦322832 was \add ≈kept there¦322842\add* in an \add ≈underground cell\add* for \add ≈several\add* days¦322844.
\p
\v 17 Then King¦322849 Tsidkiyah¦322850 sent¦322848 \add >someone\add* to fetch \add @Yirmeyah¦322862\add*, and in his house¦322854, the king¦322866 \add ≈asked¦322852\add* him privately, “Is¦322857 there¦322857 any message¦322858 from¦322859 Yahweh¦322860?”
\p “There¦322863 is¦322863 a message,” Jeremiah \add ≈answered\add*. “You'll be \add ≈handed over\add* to the Babylonian king.”
\v 18 Then¦322877 Yirmeyah¦322873 asked \add *the¦322876 king¦322876\add*, “What¦322878 \add ≈crime have¦322879 I¦322879 committed against\add* you or your servants¦322881 or your people¦322882, that¦322883 you've \add ≈had me¦322887 put¦322886 in prison\add*?
\v 19 Where¦322893 are¦322895 \add ≈all the other\add* prophets¦322895 who¦322896 prophesied¦322898 to you all that¦322910 the Babylonian¦322906 king¦322904 wouldn't come¦322903 \add ≈here\add*?
\v 20 \add ≈But¦322912\add* now¦322912, my¦322916 master¦322916 the king¦322917, please¦322920 listen¦322913 \add ≈to this appeal\add*: Don't¦322923 return me¦322925 to the scribe¦322928 Yonatan's¦322927 house¦322926, or I'll¦322930 die¦322930 there¦322931.”
\p
\v 21 \add ≈So¦322933\add* King¦322934 Tsidkiyah¦322935 ordered¦322933 that Yirmeyah \add ≈be held\add* in the guards' courtyard, and¦322933 he was given¦322942 a loaf¦322944 of bread every day¦322947 from¦322948 the bakers' street¦322948, until¦322950 \add the time\add* when all¦322953 the bread in the city¦322958 \add ≈ran out\add*. \add ≈But¦322933\add* Yirmeyah remained¦322959 \add confined\add* in the guards's courtyard.
\c 38
\s1 Yirmeyah is placed down a shaft
\rem /s1 Jeremiah in a Cistern; Jeremiah Thrown Into a Cistern; Jeremiah in the Cistern; Jeremiah in a Dry Well
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add Four officials,\add* Mattan's¦322968 son Shefatyah¦322965, Pashhur's¦322972 son Gedalyah¦322969, Shelemyah's¦322976 son Yehukal, and¦322964 Malkiyah's¦322980 son Pashhur heard the messages¦322983 that¦322984 Yirmeyah¦322985 was¦322986 telling¦322986 all¦322989 the people¦322991, saying¦322992:
\v 2 Yahweh¦322997 says¦322996 this: Anyone¦322998 who stays in¦322999 this city¦322999 will be killed by \add ≈fighting\add*, famine¦323003, or \add ≈deadly diseases\add*, \add ≈but¦323004\add* anyone¦322998 who goes¦323005 out¦323005 to¦323006 the¦323008 \add ≈Babylonians¦323008\add* will \add ≈survive—they won't be killed\add*.
\v 3 Yahweh¦323021 says¦323020 that¦323025 this¦323025 city¦323024 will¦323023 definitely \add ≈be¦323023 taken over and captured¦323031\add* by the Babylonian¦323030 king¦323028.
\p
\v 4 \add ≈So¦323033\add* \add &those\add* officials¦323034 went to¦323035 \add @King¦323037 Tsidkiyah\add* \add ≈and requested that Yirmeyah be¦323038 executed\add* because¦323044 \add (they claimed)\add* his messages were \add ≈discouraging\add* their warriors¦323055 \add ≈defending\add* the city¦323059 and \add ≡discouraging\add* all¦323063 the people. \add ≡They claimed\add* that he wasn't \add ≈advancing\add* the people's safety, but¦323033 \add causing\add* harm¦323082.
\p
\v 5 “\add ≈All right\add*,” King¦323085 Tsidkiyah¦323086 \add ≈replied\add*. “\add ≈Do whatever you want with him\add*, because¦323091 no king¦323085 \add ≈can argue against all of¦323090\add* you.”
\v 6 \add ≈So¦323099\add* they took¦323099 Yirmeyah and \add ≈put\add* him¦323104 into the \add water storage\add* cistern \add carved out by\add* the king's son Malkiyah¦323109. It was \add right there\add* in the guards' courtyard¦323114, and they lowered Yirmeyah down with¦323120 ropes¦323120. There wasn't¦323122 any water \add left\add* in the cistern, but¦323099 it was \add still\add* muddy \add at the bottom\add* and he¦323129 sank¦323129 down into the mud¦323131.
\rem /s1 Jeremiah Is Rescued by Ebed-melech
\p
\v 7 \add ≈Now\add* the Kushite Eved¦323135-Melek¦323137 was one of¦323139 the \add ≈trusted servants\add* in the king's¦323143 house¦323142 and he heard that¦323144 they¦323146 had¦323146 put¦323146 Yirmeyah¦323149 down into¦323150 the cistern¦323152. \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* the king was sitting¦323154 at the Benyamin¦323156 Gate¦323155.
\v 8 \add ≈So¦323158\add* Eved¦323159-Melek¦323161 left the \add ≈palace\add* and \add ≈went¦323158 and spoke¦323164 with\add* the king¦323167,
\v 9 “My master¦323170 the king¦323171, those men¦323173 have¦323172 been evil¦323172 in the way they've¦323172 mistreated the prophet¦323181 Yirmeyah¦323180. They threw¦323185 him into¦323186 a cistern¦323188 so he'd die¦323189 in it from¦323191 hunger, since there's no food¦323195 left in the city¦323197.”
\v 10 Then¦323199 the king ordered¦323199 Eved¦323202-Melek¦323204 to take¦323207 command¦323199 of thirty¦323210 of \add the king's men\add* to go and¦323199 get the prophet¦323216 Yirmeyah¦323215 out of the cistern¦323219 \add ≈so he¦323221 wouldn't die¦323221\add* \add down there\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈So¦323223\add* Eved¦323225-Melek¦323227 \add ≈led\add* the men¦323230 to a storeroom¦323239 for clothing under¦323238 the king's¦323235 house¦323233 where they got some rags¦323246 and¦323223 worn-out clothes. Then¦323223 they let¦323247 them¦323247 down¦323247 by ropes¦323254 to Yirmeyah¦323250 in the cistern¦323253
\v 12 and \add ≈told him to use the rags¦323268 and old clothes¦323267 under his armpits to protect him from being hurt by\add* the ropes¦323273. Yirmeyah¦323263 did that,
\v 13 then¦323278 they pulled him up with¦323282 the ropes¦323282—\add ≈that's how they got him up out\add* from¦323285 the \add mud in\add* the cistern¦323287. Then¦323278 he stayed in the guards' courtyard¦323290.
\s1 King Tsidkiyah's advice to Yirmeyah
\rem /s1 Zedekiah Consults Jeremiah Again; Zedekiah Asks Jeremiah's Advice; Zedekiah Questions Jeremiah Again; Zedekiah Questions Jeremiah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 14 \add ≈One day\add* King¦323295 Tsidkiyah \add !(Zedekiah¦323296)\add* \add ≈summoned\add* the prophet¦323301 Yirmeyah¦323300 \add ≈to meet him\add* at the third¦323306 entrance¦323305 to \add ≈the temple\add* and told him, “I¦323316 want to ask¦323315 you¦323317 something. Don't¦323319 \add ≈refuse to answer honestly and truthfully\add*.”
\p
\v 15 “\add Ha,\add* if I tell¦323331 you the truth, you'll¦323339 order me¦323335 to¦323335 be executed,” Yirmeyah¦323326 \add ≈replied\add*. “And¦323336 if I give you good advice, you won't¦323333 \add ≈take any notice of\add* what I say¦323325.”
\p
\v 16 \add ≈But¦323342\add* King¦323343 Tsidkiyah¦323344 privately promised Yirmeyah¦323347, “As¦323368 \add ≈our creator¦323361\add* Yahweh¦323352 lives¦323361, I¦323365 won't execute you or \add ≈hand¦323369 you over to\add* those men¦323370 who¦323355 \add ≈want to see you dead\add*.”
\p
\v 17 “\add Okay,\add*” Yirmeyah¦323380 \add ≈answered\add* \add *the king\add*, “Yisrael's¦323391 god, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦323387 says¦323386 this: If¦323392 you indeed¦323394 go¦323395 out¦323395 to¦323396 the Babylonian king's¦323399 officials, then you'll¦323395 live, and this city¦323404 won't¦323406 be¦323407 burnt¦323407 \add down\add*. You and your¦323411 family would live.
\v 18 But¦323413 if¦323413 you don't¦323414 go¦323416 out¦323416 to \add *his\add* officials, then¦323413 this city¦323423 will¦323422 be \add ≈handed over to the Babylonians\add*. They'll burn¦323427 it¦323427 \add down\add*, and¦323413 you wouldn't \add be able to\add* escape¦323432 from¦323433 their¦323433 \add ≈power\add*.”
\p
\v 19 “\add But\add* I'm¦323442 afraid of the \add ≈Judaneans\add* who've \add already\add* deserted to the Babylonians,” \add *the king¦323437\add* \add ≈confided to\add* Yirmeyah¦323441. “\add ≈You see,\add* I might be \add ≈handed over to them\add* and¦323457 they¦323457 \add ≈might treat me¦323459 cruelly\add*.”
\p
\v 20 “\add @The¦323470 Babylonians\add* won't¦323464 \add ≈hand\add* you over to \add @those Jews\add*,” Yirmeyah¦323463 \add ≈responded¦323462\add*. “Obey Yahweh's¦323471 message from Yahweh that I'm¦323473 \add ≈passing on to\add* you, so that things will go¦323476 well¦323476 for¦323477 you, and¦323478 so that you'll live¦323478 \add through this\add*.
\v 21 \add ≈However,\add* if¦323481 you¦323484 refuse¦323483 to¦323485 \add ≈surrender\add*, then¦323481 this¦323486 is¦323487 what Yahweh¦323490 has¦323489 shown¦323489 me¦323489:
\v 22 Listen king of Yehudah¦323501, all the women who¦323496 are¦323497 left¦323497 in¦323498 your¦323517 \add ≈palace\add* will be¦323502 taken out¦323502 to¦323503 the Babylonian king's¦323506 commanders¦323505. Those women will tell¦323509 you,
\q1 ‘You were deceived by your friends—they've¦323518 ruined you.
\q1 Now your feet¦323517 are \add ≈stuck\add* in the¦323495 mud, and¦323492 your friends have¦323518 turned¦323518 away.’
\p
\v 23 \add ≈Yes,\add* all¦323523 your¦323525 wives¦323525 and children¦323528 will be taken out¦323529 to¦323530 the \add ≈Babylonians\add* and you¦323536 yourself won't¦323534 escape¦323536 from¦323537 \add ≈them\add* \add either\add*. You'll be taken captive by¦323539 the Babylonian king¦323540, and this¦323547 city¦323546 will be burnt¦323548 \add down\add*.”
\p
\v 24 Then Tsidkiyah¦323553 told Yirmeyah¦323556, “Don't¦323558 \add ≈tell anyone¦323557 else what we spoke about or you¦323565 might\add* die¦323565.
\v 25 If the officials¦323570 hear¦323569 that¦323571 I've¦323573 have¦323573 talked with¦323574 you, and if they¦323575 come¦323575 and \add ≈demand\add*, ‘Tell¦323579 us what¦323583 you said to¦323586 the king—don't¦323589 hide¦323591 it from us or we'll¦323594 kill you,’
\v 26 then¦323601 you¦323601 must¦323601 tell them¦323602, ‘I \add ≈was¦323603 just pleading\add* to the king¦323608 not¦323609 to return me¦323610 to \add the dungeon in\add* Yonatan's¦323612 house¦323611 \add ≈or I'd\add* die¦323613 there¦323614.’
\v 27 Then \add sure enough\add* the officials¦323620 came¦323617 to¦323621 Yirmeyah¦323623 and questioned him and he¦323626 \add ≈answered\add* them¦323627 as the king¦323634 had¦323633 \add ≈instructed¦323633\add* him. They couldn't say anything else because¦323637 they hadn't heard¦323640 the \add ≈conversation\add*,
\v 28 \add ≈so\add* Yirmeyah¦323645 remained¦323644 in¦323646 the guards' courtyard¦323646 until¦323648 the day¦323650 that Yerushalem¦323654 was captured.\x + \xo 38:28: \xt Eze 33:21.\x*
\c 39
\s1 The fall of Yerushalem
\rem /s1 The Fall of Jerusalem
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 In¦323662 the tenth¦323669 month¦323668 of the ninth¦323663 year¦323662 \add of the reign\add* of Yehudah's¦323667 King Tsidkiyah \add !(Zedekiah¦323664)\add*, the Babylonian King Nebuchadnezzar¦323671 came¦323670 against Yerushalem¦323680 with his¦323677 \add ≈large\add* army¦323677 and¦323681 besieged it¦323682.
\v 2 On the ninth day¦323692 of the fourth¦323691 month of Tsidkiyah's¦323689 eleventh year¦323688,\f + \fr 39:2 \ft i.e., about eighteen months later (in 586 B.C.).\f* the city¦323695 was¦323694 broken¦323694 into¦323694.
\v 3 Then¦323697 all¦323698 of the Babylonian king's¦323700 officials¦323729 came¦323697 and sat at the middle¦323705 gate¦323704, \add including\add* the top official Nevu-Sarsekim, and Samgar¦323710-Nevu and Sarsekim.
\p
\v 4 When¦323733 Yehudah's¦323739 King¦323737 Tsidkiyah¦323736 and all¦323740 his warriors¦323742 saw¦323735 \add what was happening\add*, they \add left\add* at nighttime¦323746 through the gate¦323753 between¦323754 the two¦323755 walls¦323755 beside the king's¦323752 garden¦323751 and fled¦323744 towards the Yarden¦323758 river plains.
\v 5 \add ≈However\add* the \add ≈Babylonian\add* army¦323761 chased after¦323764 them¦323764 and overtook¦323765 the king¦323777 down in the plains¦323769 near Yeriho¦323770 \add !(Jericho¦323770)\add*. They took¦323771 him back up¦323773 to¦323774 the Babylonian King¦323777 Nebuchadnezzar¦323776 at Rivlah¦323780 in the Hamat¦323782 \add ≈region¦323781\add*, and he¦323783 pronounced \add &his\add* judgement¦323785 on him.
\v 6 The¦323788 king¦323788 had Tsidkiyah's¦323793 sons¦323792 slaughtered¦323787 at¦323794 Rivlah¦323794 as \add @their father\add* \add was forced to\add* watch, and¦323787 Yehudah's¦323800 officials were also executed.
\v 7 Then¦323805 they \add ≈gouged out\add* out Tsidkiyah's¦323808 eyes¦323807 and¦323810 put him¦323810 in chains to be taken to Babylon¦323814.
\v 8 Then¦323816 the Babylonians¦323825 burnt¦323824 down the \add ≈palace\add* and the \add ≈other\add* houses¦323822, and tore down Yerushalem's¦323830 walls¦323829.
\v 9 The¦323834 rest¦323834 of the people¦323835 who'd stayed in¦323837 the city¦323837, including¦323838 those¦323840 who'd \add ≈previously\add* deserted, were exiled¦323848 to Babylon¦323856 \add under the supervision of\add* the chief¦323853 bodyguard¦323855 Nevuzar-Adan.
\v 10 \add ≈However¦323868,\add* \add *he\add* allowed the poorest people¦323860 who¦323862 didn't¦323863 own anything¦323866 to remain in Yehudah¦323873—allocating vineyards¦323876 and¦323858 fields¦323877 \add for them to work\add*.
\s1 Yirmeyah is released
\rem /s1 Jeremiah, Set Free, Remembers Ebed-melech; Jeremiah's Release; Jeremiah Remains in Judah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 11 \add ≈Now\add* the Babylonian King¦323883 Nebuchadnezzar¦323882 had given an order to¦323894 his chief¦323891 bodyguard¦323893 Nevuzar-Adan about \add finding\add* Yirmeyah¦323888
\v 12 and keeping him safe and unharmed—even to¦323903 care for him and do¦323913 anything¦323904 that he¦323910 requested.
\v 13 \add ≈So¦323916\add* Nevuzar-Adan, the top servant Nevu-Shazban, the high official Nergal¦323926-Sharezer, and¦323916 all¦323933 the Babylonian king's¦323935 most important officials
\v 14 sent¦323939 out men to fetch Yirmeyah from¦323944 the guards' courtyard¦323944. They¦323946 \add ≈handed him over\add* to Gedalyah¦323950 (son of Ahikam¦323953, son of Shafan¦323956) to take¦323957 him home, \add ≈so\add* Yirmeyah stayed \add there\add* among the people¦323963.
\s1 Hope for Eved-Melek
\rem /s1 Hope for Ebedmelech
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 15 \add ≈While\add* Yirmeyah¦323968 had still been \add ≈held\add* in¦323975 the guards' courtyard¦323975, Yahweh¦323972 had given him this message¦323970:
\v 16 Go and tell Eved¦323981-Melek the \add ≈Ethiopian¦323985\add* that Yisrael's¦323993 god¦323992, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦323990 says¦323989 this: Listen, I'm¦323994 about¦323995 to \add ≈fulfill\add* my¦323999 messages¦323999 against¦324000 this city¦324002 for disaster and not¦324005 for good¦324006, and they'll¦324007 all come true \add ≈right in front¦324008 of your¦324008 eyes\add* on that day¦324009.
\v 17 \add ≈But¦324012\add* Yahweh¦324018 declares that I'll¦324012 rescue¦324012 you from those people¦324022 that you're¦324025 afraid of
\v 18 because I'll¦324031 definitely save your life. You¦324031 won't¦324033 \add ≈be killed by¦324032 the soldiers\add*, but¦324032 Yahweh¦324045 declares that because you¦324041 put your trust¦324041 in¦324042 me¦324042, your life will be saved.
\c 40
\s1 Yirmeyah returns to Gedalyah
\rem /s1 Jeremiah Freed; Jeremiah Stays with Gedaliah; After the capture of Jerusalem; Jeremiah with Gedaliah the Governor
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 The chief¦324062 bodyguard¦324064 Nevuzar-Adan had found Yirmeyah¦324054 \add ≈chained¦324073 up\add* among all the exiles¦324077 from¦324065 Yerushalem¦324078 and \add the rest of\add* Yehudah¦324079 to be taken¦324080 to Babylon¦324081, and had released him at Ramah¦324067.
\p
\v 2 The chief¦324084 bodyguard¦324086 took¦324083 Yirmeyah¦324087 \add aside\add* and¦324088 told him¦324089, “Your¦324091 god¦324091 Yahweh¦324090 decreed this disaster for this place¦324099,
\v 3 then¦324102 he caused it to happen. Yahweh¦324104 did just¦324105 as¦324105 he'd decreed, since you \add >people\add* sinned¦324109 against him and¦324102 didn't¦324111 obey \add ≈him\add*. That's¦324110 why \add all\add* this has happened to you people.
\v 4 \add ≈But¦324121\add* now¦324121 listen, I've¦324123 released you today from¦324125 your¦324131 chains¦324127. If¦324132 \add ≈you choose\add* to come with me to Babylon¦324138, I'll¦324140 \add ≈look after\add* you, \add ≈but¦324121 if you don't want to\add*, then¦324121 look \add ≈around\add* and¦324121 go \add ≈wherever you think best\add*.
\v 5 \add ?≈Or why don't¦324171 you return\add* to¦324175 Gedalyah¦324177 (son of Ahikam¦324180, son of Shafan¦324183) who the Babylonian king has¦324185 put in charge of Yehudah's¦324190 cities¦324189. Stay among the people¦324194 with¦324192 him, or¦324195 go wherever \add ≈you think best\add*.” Then¦324170 the the king's chief¦324207 bodyguard¦324209 gave¦324204 him food¦324210 and a gift, and sent¦324212 him away.
\v 6 \add ≈So¦324214\add* Yirmeyah¦324215 went¦324214 to Gedalyah's¦324218 \add place\add* and¦324223 stayed with¦324224 him¦324224 among the people¦324226 who were left behind in¦324225 the land.
\s1 Yehudah's governor Gedalyah
\rem /s1 Gedaliah Assassinated; Gedaliah, Governor of Judah; Gedaliah Governs in Judah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (2 Kgs 25:22-24)
\p
\v 7 \add ≈Now some\add* commanders¦324234 of \add Judean\add* \add ≈soldiers\add* who were still in the countryside¦324237, along with their¦324239 men heard that the Babylonian king¦324243 had¦324242 made Ahikam's¦324251 son¦324249 Gedalyah¦324248 governor over the land. They also heard that he'd put him in charge of the men, women¦324258, and children who were the poorest people¦324260 in the land—those¦324262 who hadn't been¦324265 exiled¦324265 to¦324266 Babylon¦324245.\x + \xo 40:7-9: \xt 2Ki 25:22-24.\x*
\v 8 \add ≈So¦324268\add* they¦324268 went to Gedalyah¦324271 at Mitspah¦324272. Those \add ≈who went\add* were Netanyah's¦324276 son Yishmael¦324273, Kareah's¦324281 sons Yohanan¦324277 and Yonatan¦324278, Tanhumet's¦324285 son Serayah¦324282, the sons of¦324288 Ofai the Netofatite, and Maakati's¦324294 son Yezanyah¦324291, and their¦324296 men¦324296.
\v 9 Gedalyah¦324300 (son of Ahikam¦324303, son of Shafan¦324306) \add made a promise\add* to them and their¦324307 men¦324307, saying¦324308, “Don't¦324309 be afraid¦324311 to serve the \add ≈Babylonian\add* officials. Live in¦324315 the land and serve the Babylonian king¦324319, and it¦324321 will go¦324321 well¦324321 with you.
\v 10 See, I'm living¦324326 in Mitspah¦324327 to meet with the \add ≈Babylonians\add* who¦324331 came¦324332 to us¦324333. \add ≈So¦324324\add* harvest wine¦324336, summer¦324337 fruit¦324337, and oil¦324338 and store them¦324339 in your containers. Live in the cities¦324342 that¦324343 you've \add ≈occupied\add*.”
\v 11 Then¦324347 all¦324348 the Judeans in Moav¦324353, among¦324355 the people of Ammon¦324357, and in Edom¦324358, and in every land heard¦324363 that the Babylonian king¦324367 had allowed a \add ≈small number of people\add* to¦324371 stay in Yehudah¦324371, and that he'd appointed¦324373 Gedalyah¦324377 (son of Ahikam¦324380, son of Shafan¦324383) over them.
\v 12 \add ≈So¦324385\add* all¦324386 the¦324388 Judeans¦324388 from¦324389 every place¦324391 that they'd be driven¦324393 into, came¦324396 \add back\add* to Yehudah¦324399 to Gedalyah¦324402 at Mitspah¦324403, and they \add ≈harvested a lot\add* of wine¦324405 and summer¦324406 fruit¦324406.
\s1 The murder of Gedalyah
\rem /s1 Gedaliah Is Murdered; A Plot against Gedaliah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (2 Kgs 25:25-26)
\p
\v 13 \add Some time later,\add* Kareah's¦324414 son¦324412 Yonatan and all¦324415 the army commanders¦324417 from the countryside¦324420, came¦324421 to Gedalyah¦324424 at Mitspah¦324425,
\v 14 and¦324427 \add ≈asked\add* him¦324428, “Do¦324431 you realise that¦324432 the Ammonite King¦324435 Baalis¦324433 has¦324439 sent¦324439 Netanyah's¦324445 son Yishmael¦324442 to¦324446 \add ≈assassinate\add* you?” \add ≈However\add* Ahikim's son Gedaliah¦324452 didn't¦324448 believe¦324450 them
\v 15 \add ≈so\add* Kareah's¦324460 son¦324458 Yohanan spoke privately to Gedalyah¦324464 at¦324466 Mitspah¦324466, “Allow me to go¦324468 \add and\add* kill Netanyah's¦324476 Yishmael¦324473. No one will suspect me. Why should¦324468 he kill you? Why allow all¦324484 of¦324484 Yehudah¦324486 that has¦324487 been gathered¦324487 to you to be scattered¦324483 and the¦324490 remnant¦324490 destroyed?”
\p
\v 16 \add ≈However\add* Ahikam's¦324497 son Gedalyah¦324494 \add ≈replied\add* to¦324498 Kareah's¦324503 son Yohanan¦324500, “\add No,\add* don't¦324504 do that¦324511, because¦324512 you're¦324515 lying about¦324517 Yishmael¦324519.”
\c 41
\rem /s1 Insurrection against Gedaliah; The Murder of Gedaliah
\p
\v 1 \add ≈However,\add* in¦324524 the seventh¦324525 month¦324524, Yishmael¦324527 (son of Netanyah¦324530, son of Elishama from the royal¦324535 family) and some officers of the king¦324537 came—he had ten¦324538 men¦324539 with¦324540 him¦324540. \add ≡They came\add* to¦324541 Ahikam's¦324546 son Gedalyah¦324543 at Mitspah¦324547 and \add ≈had a meal\add* together¦324551.\x + \xo 41:1-3: \xt 2Ki 25:25.\x*
\v 2 Then¦324554 Yishmael and the ten¦324559 men¦324560 who were¦324564 with him¦324565, \add ≈stood\add* up and attacked with their swords¦324576. Yishmael killed¦324577 Gedalyah¦324569, who the Babylonian king¦324582 had¦324581 put in charge of¦324582 the \add ≈region\add*,
\v 3 and¦324587 they killed all¦324588 the Judeans who were with Gedalyah¦324597 \add there\add* at¦324598 Mitspah¦324598, as well as the Babylonian soldiers who were there.
\p
\v 4 The \add ≈next\add* day¦324613 \add ≈before anyone¦324619 found out that Gedalyah¦324618 had been murdered¦324615\add*,
\v 5 eighty¦324628 men¦324624 from Shekem¦324625, Shiloh¦324626, and¦324623 from Shomron¦324627 came¦324623 who had¦324634 shaved¦324630 off their beards¦324631, torn¦324632 their clothes¦324633, and cut¦324634 themselves¦324634 \add in mourning\add*. They were carrying grain offerings¦324635 and incense to¦324638 \add ≈be offered¦324635 at\add* Yahweh's¦324640 \add ≈residence\add*.
\v 6 Netanyah's¦324646 son Yishmael¦324643 went out¦324642 of¦324644 Mitspah¦324650 to meet¦324647 them, weeping¦324653 as he went. \add ≈When¦324642 he reached\add* them, he told them to come¦324659 and¦324642 see what had happened to Ahikam's¦324665 son Gedalyah¦324662.
\v 7 Then¦324678 as¦324669 they¦324669 \add ≈reached\add* the middle¦324672 of¦324672 the town¦324673, Yishmael¦324675 and his men¦324684 slaughtered¦324674 them¦324674 \add and threw their bodies\add* into a cistern¦324682.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈However,\add* ten¦324689 of them \add ≈bargained with Yishmael¦324697 about some\add* wheat¦324708, barley¦324709, oil¦324710, and¦324689 honey¦324711 \add ≈that they'd left out\add* in¦324707 the countryside¦324707, \add ≈so\add* he didn't¦324698 kill¦324700 them along with the others.
\v 9 The¦324718 \add water storage\add* cistern¦324718 when Yishmael had thrown¦324720 all¦324725 the¦324727 bodies of¦324727 those¦324750 he'd killed \add ?≈including\add* Gedalyah¦324733, had been dug by¦324731 King Asa¦324738 \add ≈in¦324739 defence against\add* Yisrael's¦324743 King Baasha¦324740. \add ≈Now\add* Netanyah's¦324749 son¦324747 Yishmael had filled¦324745 it¦324744 \add ≈with dead bodies\add*.
\v 10 Next Yishmael captured the remaining¦324772 people¦324760 in¦324762 Mitspah¦324762, \add ≈including¦324767\add* the king's¦324766 daughters¦324765 and¦324752 all¦324769 the others who the chief¦324777 bodyguard¦324779 Nevuzar-Adan had¦324775 assigned to Ahikam's¦324785 son Gedalyah¦324782. \add ≈So¦324752\add* Netanyah's¦324790 son Yishmael captured them to hand over¦324792 to the \add ≈Ammonites\add*.
\p
\v 11 \add ≈Meanwhile\add* Kareah's¦324803 son Yohanan¦324800 and¦324804 all the army commanders¦324806 with¦324809 him¦324809, heard about all the evil¦324813 \add >things\add* that¦324814 Netanyah's¦324819 son Yishmael¦324816 had¦324815 done¦324815,
\v 12 \add ≈so\add* they¦324821 took¦324821 all¦324824 their men¦324826 to¦324828 fight against Yishmael¦324831. They¦324835 \add ≈came across\add* him¦324836 at the large¦324840 pool \add ≈near\add* Giv'on \add city\add*
\v 13 \add ≈When¦324844\add* all the people¦324848 who'd \add ≈been captured by\add* Yishmael¦324852 saw¦324845 Yohanan¦324855 and¦324844 all the army commanders¦324862 they¦324866 were \add ≈very relieved\add*.
\v 14 \add ≈So¦324868\add* all¦324869 \add &those\add* people¦324871 that¦324872 Yishmael¦324875 had¦324874 captured \add ≈were freed\add* and¦324868 went¦324880 \add ≈back¦324879\add* with Kareah's¦324886 son¦324884 Yohanan¦324883.
\v 15 \add ≈Unfortunately,\add* Netanyah's¦324891 son¦324889 Yishmael¦324888 escaped¦324892 from Yohanan¦324896, along with eight¦324893 of¦324895 his men¦324894, and¦324897 they went¦324897 to¦324898 the¦324900 Ammonites.
\rem /s1 Flight to Egypt
\p
\v 16 Then Kareah's¦324908 son Yohanan¦324905 and all the army commanders¦324911 with¦324915 him¦324915, took all the people¦324920 from Mitspah¦324930 who'd been \add ≈rescued\add* from Netanyah's¦324927 son Yishmael¦324924 after¦324931 he'd killed Ahikam's¦324938 son Gedalyah¦324935. \add ≡They took\add* \add &those\add* warriors¦324939, and women¦324942 and children and court-officials¦324944 that¦324921 they'd \add ≈saved at Giv'on\add*,
\v 17 and went¦324949 and stayed at¦324951 Gerut¦324951-Kimham near Beyt¦324957-Lehem, \add ≈getting ready\add* to go¦324959 to Egypt¦324961
\v 18 because of¦324963 the \add ≈Babylonians\add*. (They¦324966 \add ≈worried about their¦324967 response\add* because Netanyah's¦324974 son Yishmael¦324971 had \add ≈assassinated\add* Ahikam's¦324980 son Gedalyah¦324977 who'd been appointed¦324983 in the \add ≈region\add* by the Babylonian king¦324984.)
\c 42
\s1 The people ask Yirmeyah to pray
\rem /s1 The People Ask Jeremiah to Pray for Them; Warning to Stay in Judah; Jeremiah Advises Survivors Not to Migrate
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 Then all the army commanders¦324993, as well as Kareah's¦324998 son Yohanan¦324995, Hoshayah's¦325002 son Yezanyah¦324999, and¦325003 all the people¦325005 from¦325006 the less \add ≈prominent\add* to the \add ≈most important officials\add* approached¦324990 the prophet Yirmeyah
\v 2 and¦325011 \add ≈asked\add* him, “Please \add ≈listen to our request\add*. \add ≡Please\add* ask your god¦325026 Yahweh¦325025 our on behalf of \add ≈all¦325028 of us who are¦325034 left here, because¦325032 there's not very many¦325036 of us left as you can see¦325039\add*.
\v 3 Ask your¦325046 god¦325046 Yahweh¦325045 to¦325044 tell us¦325044 what we should do¦325058 and¦325054 where we should go¦325051.”
\p
\v 4 “\add Sure,\add* I've¦325064 heard¦325064 \add your concerns\add*,” the prophet¦325063 Yirmeyah¦325062 \add ≈responded¦325060\add*. “Listen, Ill pray¦325066 to your god¦325070 Yahweh as you've all requested. Whatever Yahweh answers¦325078, I'll tell¦325081 you. I'll keep nothing back from¦325086 you all.”
\p
\v 5 ⇔“We \add promise\add* to do everything¦325103 that¦325106 your¦325109 god¦325109 Yahweh tells us to do,” they told Yirmeyah¦325093. “If¦325100 we¦325112 don't¦325102, then¦325089 Yahweh can be a true and¦325089 faithful¦325099 witness¦325097 against us.
\v 6 Whether¦325114 it's good¦325116 or bad¦325119, we'll¦325130 obey the¦325120 \add ≈instructions from\add* our god Yahweh¦325122 who we're¦325125 \add ≈asking you¦325128 to speak\add* to, so¦325131 that it may¦325133 be well¦325133 with us¦325135 when we obey \add *his\add* \add ≈response\add*.”
\s1 Yahweh's answer to Yirmeyah's prayer
\rem /s1 The Lord's Answer to Jeremiah's Prayer
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 7 After ten¦325145 days¦325146, Yahweh's¦325150 \add ≈response\add* came to¦325151 Yirmeyah¦325153,
\v 8 \add ≈so\add* \add *he¦325155\add* called¦325155 Kareah's¦325161 son¦325159 Yohanan¦325158 and¦325155 all the army commanders¦325165, as well as all the people¦325171 from¦325172 the less \add ≈prominent\add* to the \add ≈most important officials\add*,
\v 9 then¦325177 he¦325177 told them¦325178, “You all sent¦325186 me¦325187 to Yisrael's¦325184 god¦325183 Yahweh¦325182 \add ≈to pass on your requests\add* \add ≈and¦325177 here's his reply\add*:
\v 10 If you all stay in this¦325198 \add ≈region\add*, then I'll build¦325199 you up¦325199 and not tear¦325202 you down¦325202. I'll plant¦325203 you and not pull you all out, because¦325207 I'm¦325208 upset about¦325209 the¦325211 harm¦325211 that¦325212 I've¦325213 done¦325213 to¦325214 you all.
\v 11 Don't be afraid of the¦325220 Babylonian king¦325220 \add ≈any more\add*. This is Yahweh's¦325233 declaration: Don't be afraid of him¦325226 because¦325234 I'm with¦325236 you all to save¦325238 you and¦325240 to rescue¦325240 you from¦325242 his¦325226 \add ≈clutches\add*,
\v 12 because I'll give¦325244 you all mercy. I'll have¦325247 compassion¦325247 on¦325247 you, and¦325244 I'll restore¦325249 you all back to¦325251 your \add ≈country\add*.
\p
\v 13 \add ≈However,\add* suppose that¦325262 you all decide not to listen¦325264 to the¦325265 \add ≈words\add* of your god¦325267 Yahweh¦325266, and¦325255 \add ≈decide\add* not to stay in this \add ≈region\add*,
\v 14 \add and\add* if you all say¦325269 that you'll go¦325274 to Egypt¦325273 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add* to live there where¦325275 there's no war, and no trumpets¦325281 \add ≈signalling\add*, and no \add ≈shortage of\add* food¦325284,
\v 15 Now¦325291 \add you\add* \add ≈remaining people\add* listen¦325293 to Yahweh's¦325296 message¦325294: Yisrael's¦325305 god¦325304, Commander-in-chief Yahweh says¦325301 that if¦325306 you all \add ≈do decide\add* to go \add ≈and¦325291 stay\add* \add down\add* in Egypt¦325313,
\v 16 then the¦325319 \add ≈war\add* that you all fear will overtake¦325325 you in¦325327 Egypt. The¦325329 famine¦325329 that you're anxious¦325334 about will follow you all to Egypt, and¦325318 then you'll die¦325341 there¦325340,
\v 17 \add ≈i.e.,\add* \add ≈anyone who¦325347 decides\add* to go¦325353 to \add ≈live as foreigners\add* in Egypt¦325354, will die¦325357 from \add ≈war\add*, famine¦325359, or \add ≈deadly diseases\add*. There won't¦325361 be any survivors¦325365 from the¦325368 \add #calamities¦325368\add* that¦325369 I'd \add ≈send\add* onto them¦325372.
\p
\v 18 \add ≈Yes,\add* Yisrael's¦325381 god¦325380, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦325378 says¦325377 this: Just¦325382 as my anger and rage was¦325383 poured out on Yerushalem's¦325389 inhabitants¦325388, in the¦325388 same way my anger would be poured out on all of you if you go¦325394 to Egypt¦325395. You'd become an object of cursing and a horror¦325398, \add ≈something to be used as a curse word\add*, and something dishonourable, and you'd never see¦325403 this place¦325407 again¦325404.
\p
\v 19 \add Then Yirmeyah continued:\add* Yahweh¦325411 has¦325410 spoken¦325410 to you all, the \add ≈remaining people\add* of¦325413 Yehudah¦325414. Don't¦325415 go¦325417 \add down\add* to Egypt¦325418 as you know that I've¦325423 definitely warned¦325423 you all \add against that\add* today.
\v 20 \add ≈Yes,\add* you \add ≈made a life and death mistake\add* when you sent¦325435 me to your god¦325440 Yahweh¦325439, and \add ≈asked me to ask him for instructions for you\add* and when you all¦325448 said that you'd do¦325457 everything that \add *he¦325450\add* says,
\v 21 because I've¦325459 reported \add >all that\add* to you today. \add ≈However,\add* you haven't listened¦325463 to your god¦325466 Yahweh's¦325465 message, or to anything that he¦325470 sent¦325470 me¦325470 \add to tell\add* you all about.
\v 22 \add ≈So¦325473\add* now¦325473, you should definitely \add ≈be aware\add* that¦325476 you'll die¦325480 from \add ≈war\add*, famine¦325478, and \add ≈deadly diseases\add* where¦325482 you all wanted to go¦325484 and \add ≈live as foreigners\add*.
\c 43
\s1 Yirmeyah gets taken to Egypt
\rem /s1 Taken to Egypt, Jeremiah Warns of Judgment; Jeremiah Taken to Egypt; Jeremiah Is Taken to Egypt
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add ≈When\add* Yirmeyah¦325491 had finished¦325490 \add ≈passing on\add* Yahweh's¦325503 messages¦325502 that¦325505 their god Yahweh had told him¦325506 to¦325509 say,
\v 2 Hoshayah's¦325521 son Azaryah¦325518, Kareah's¦325525 son Yohanan¦325522, and all¦325526 the arrogant¦325529 men told Yirmeyah¦325533, “You're \add ≈lying\add* \add to us\add*. Our god¦325540 Yahweh¦325539 didn't¦325537 send¦325538 you to \add ≈tell¦325530 us\add* not¦325542 to go¦325544 \add and\add* live in Egypt¦325545.
\v 3 \add It's\add* because¦325549 Neriyah's¦325553 son¦325551 Baruk¦325550 is¦325554 inciting¦325554 you¦325555 against¦325556 us¦325556 \add so that\add* we'll \add stay here and\add* \add ≈get captured by the Babylonians\add* to be \add either\add* put¦325563 to death¦325563 or be taken¦325565 as exiles¦325565 to Babylon¦325567.”
\p
\v 4 \add ≈So¦325569\add* Kareah's¦325575 son¦325573 Yohanan¦325572, all the army officers, and¦325569 all \add the rest of\add* the people¦325582, refused to \add ≈take notice of Yahweh's¦325584 instructions\add* to \add remain\add* living in¦325586 the Yehudah¦325587 \add ≈region¦325586\add*.
\v 5 Then¦325589 Yohanan¦325590 and all the army commanders¦325596 \add ≈gathered all those remaining Judean people together, who'd come¦325605 from¦325606 all the other countries¦325608 that they'd previously been¦325610 driven¦325610 away¦325610 to and\add* returned to live in¦325614 Yehudah¦325602.\x + \xo 43:5-7: \xt 2Ki 25:26.\x*
\v 6 \add That included\add* men¦325619 and women¦325622, children, the king's daughters¦325628, and all the people that Nevuzar-Adan, the king's chief¦325637 bodyguard¦325639 Nevuzar-Adan had¦325635 left¦325635 with¦325640 Gedalyah¦325642 (son of Ahikam¦325645, son of Shafan¦325648), and including¦325620 the prophet¦325651 Yirmeyah¦325650 and Neriyah's¦325657 son Baruk¦325654.
\v 7 Then¦325659 they went¦325659 to Egypt¦325661 because¦325662 they \add ≈took no notice of¦325665 Yahweh's¦325666 instructions\add* and¦325659 they arrived at Tahpanhes¦325670.
\p
\v 8 In¦325680 Tahpanhes¦325680, Yahweh¦325676 \add ≈gave\add* Yirmeyah¦325679 a message¦325674:
\v 9 \add ≈Get\add* some large¦325686 stones¦325685 and¦325687 \add ≈while the people¦325697 from Yehudah are watching\add*, \add ≈push\add* them into the mortar¦325688 in the pavement at the entrance¦325691 to Far-oh's¦325694 \add !(Pharaoh's¦325694)\add* \add ≈palace\add* at Tahpanhes¦325695.
\v 10 Then¦325700 tell \add @the Judeans\add* that¦325724 Yisrael's¦325708 god¦325707, Commander-in-chief says¦325704: Listen, I'm¦325709 about¦325710 to send¦325710 messengers¦325706 to my servant¦325718 the Babylonian King¦325715 Nebuchadnezzar¦325714, to summon him \add here\add*. I'll¦325711 place his throne¦325720 over the top of¦325729 those hidden¦325725 stones¦325722, and¦325700 he'll¦325726 spread¦325726 his \add ≈royal\add* tent¦325729 over them¦325731.
\v 11 He'll come¦325733 here to attack¦325735 Egypt¦325739 \add ≈and he'll¦325733 kill those that¦325743 I've assigned to die, and similarly for those to be taken captive or run through with a\add* sword.
\v 12 Then¦325750 \add ?≈he'll\add* light a fire¦325751 in¦325752 the temples of Egypt's¦325754 gods¦325753. Nebuchadnezzar will¦325755 \add either\add* burn¦325755 them or \add ≈carry them away\add*. He'll clean Egypt out just like shepherds¦325765 pick lice off their clothes, and¦325750 then¦325750 he'll \add ≈quietly\add* leave
\v 13 \add after\add* smashing the stone pillars¦325776 at \add ≈Heliopolis\add* and¦325773 burning¦325789 the temples of Egypt's¦325781 gods¦325785.
\c 44
\s1 Yahweh's message to the Judeans in Egypt
\rem /s1 Denunciation of Persistent Idolatry; The Lord's Message to the Israelites in Egypt; Disaster Because of Idolatry; Judgment for Idolatry
\p
\v 1 Yahweh spoke to¦325795 Yirmeyah¦325797 about¦325798 all¦325799 the¦325801 Judeans who lived in Migdol¦325806, Tahpanhes¦325807, and¦325807 Memphis¦325808 in \add northern/lower\add* Egypt, as well as those in Patros¦325810 \add in southern/upper Egypt\add*:
\v 2 Yisrael's¦325820 god¦325819, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦325817 says¦325816 that you yourselves have¦325822 seen¦325822 all the disasters that I¦325828 \add ≈sent to\add* Yerushalem¦325831 and Yehudah's¦325836 other cities¦325835. See¦325837, they're¦325837 \add just\add* ruins¦325838 \add ≈today without anyone living in\add* them¦325842.
\v 3 \add ≈That's because\add* of the wicked¦325846 things they did¦325848 to provoke¦325849 me to anger¦325849 by going¦325850 to burn incense and¦325860 to worship other¦325854 gods¦325853 that¦325847 neither they themselves, nor you, nor your ancestors¦325860 had¦325857 \add ≈ever heard about before\add*.
\v 4 I repeatedly sent¦325862 all¦325866 my¦325868 servants¦325868, the prophets¦325869, to them to tell \add >the people\add* to stop doing those detestable things¦325878 that¦325882 I hate¦325883,
\v 5 \add ≈but¦325885\add* they¦325886 didn't¦325885 listen¦325886. They¦325889 \add ≈refused to take any notice of it, or to stop their wicked¦325894 activities like burning incense\add* to other¦325898 gods¦325897.
\v 6 \add ≈So¦325900\add* my¦325901 anger¦325902 and rage¦325901 was poured¦325900 out and burnt¦325903 in¦325904 Yehudah's¦325905 cities¦325904 and Yerushalem's¦325907 streets¦325906 \add like a fire\add* and they're \add still\add* desolate¦325910 ruins¦325909 to this¦325912 day¦325911.
\p
\v 7 \add ≈So\add* now¦325915 Yisrael's¦325923 god, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦325919 \add ≈asks\add* why¦325924 you all \add insist on\add* \add ≈bringing this terrible\add* harm¦325927 onto yourselves \add that'll see\add* men and women, children¦325937 and babies from¦325939 Yehudah¦325940, eliminated without even leaving¦325942 a remnant¦325944.
\v 8 You've provoked¦325946 me¦325946 to anger¦325946 by \add ≈what you've all done\add* with your¦325948 \add own\add* two¦325948 hands¦325948, by \add ≈burning incense\add* to other¦325951 gods¦325950 in Egypt¦325953 where¦325954 you've all gone to \add ≈live as foreigners\add*. You've cut¦325961 yourselves off¦325961 so¦325963 as to become¦325964 a curse¦325965 \add word\add* and¦325966 a reproach¦325966 among¦325967 all the nations¦325968 in the \add ≈world\add*.
\v 9 Have you all forgotten the wicked¦325974 \add >things done¦325991\add* by your ancestors¦325975 and \add also\add* by Yehudah's¦325981 kings¦325980 and their wives? Have you forgotten the evil committed by yourselves and your wives in¦325992 Yehudah and on Yerushalem's¦325995 streets¦325994?
\v 10 To this day¦326000, they still \add ≈haven't humbled themselves\add*. They don't respect \add ≈the instructions or regulations that¦326009 I¦326011 gave\add* them and their ancestors¦326014, \add ≈and so they don't follow them\add*.
\p
\v 11 Therefore Yisrael's¦326024 god¦326023, Commander-in-chief says¦326020 this: Listen, I'm¦326025 about¦326026 \add ≈to start working against\add* you all to \add ≈bring disaster\add* and¦326030 \add ≈destroy\add* all Yehudah¦326035.
\v 12 I'll \add ≈eliminate\add* the \add ≈small¦326060 group of Judeans\add* that has \add ≈made up their¦326045 minds\add* to go¦326046 to \add ≈live as foreigners\add* in¦326054 Egypt. I'll do that so that they'll all \add ≈die there¦326051\add* Egypt—from either \add ≈war\add* or famine¦326058, \add and\add* from the least to the \add ≈very prominent\add* \add >people\add* they'll die and will¦326067 become \add ≈a curse¦326068 word, a horror¦326069 story, and something to ridicule and mock\add*.
\v 13 I will¦326073 \add ≈punish\add* those¦326075 living in¦326076 Egypt¦326077 just¦326078 like I \add ≈punished\add* Yerushalem¦326082 with \add ≈war\add*, famine¦326084, and¦326073 \add ≈deadly diseases\add*
\v 14 \add ≈so that\add* none of the¦326093 \add ≈remaining people\add* from Yehudah who've gone¦326093 to live in¦326097 Egypt¦326098 will escape or survive¦326090 or \add be able to\add* return to Yehudah when they¦326105 want to return and¦326087 live there. None of them will return except a few who escaped from there.
\p
\v 15 Then all the men¦326129 who knew¦326130 that¦326146 their¦326134 wives¦326134 were \add ≈burning incense\add* to¦326135 other¦326136 gods¦326135, and all the women¦326139 who were in the great¦326142 assembly, and all the people¦326145 who were living¦326146 in Lower and Upper Egypt¦326149, answered¦326123 Yirmeyah¦326126:
\v 16 \add Concerning\add* that message¦326153 that you told us¦326157 in¦326158 Yahweh's¦326159 name¦326158, we're¦326160 not¦326160 listening¦326161 to you
\v 17 because¦326164 we'll certainly¦326165 do everything¦326169 that¦326173 \add ≈we said we'd do\add*. \add ≡We'll\add* burn incense to the queen¦326178 of the skies¦326179 and pour¦326180 out¦326180 drink¦326183 offerings¦326183 to her¦326182 just¦326184 as¦326184 we, our ancestors¦326187, our kings¦326188, and our leaders did in¦326190 Yehudah's¦326191 cities¦326190 and on Yerushalem's¦326193 streets¦326192. Then we'll \add ≈have¦326185 plenty of\add* food¦326196 and will prosper, and won't¦326200 \add ≈experience\add* distress¦326199.
\v 18 Whenever we didn't do those things—not offering¦326213 incense to the queen¦326208 of¦326208 the skies¦326209 and not pouring¦326210 out¦326210 drink¦326213 offerings¦326213 to her—we were all suffering from poverty and dying from by¦326216 \add ≈war\add* and famine¦326217.
\p
\v 19 The women said, “When¦326220 we were offering incense to the queen¦326224 of¦326224 the skies¦326225 and pouring out drink offerings to her, and when we were making¦326223 cakes¦326233 in her image and pouring out drink offerings to her, \add ≈did¦326231 you think we were doing it¦326236 behind our husbands' backs\add*?”
\p
\v 20 Then Yirmeyah¦326241 \add ≈responded¦326240 to¦326242\add* all those who'd answered¦326258 him including¦326240 both men¦326249 and women¦326252. He told them all this message¦326260:
\v 21 Didn't Yahweh¦326281 remember¦326280 the incense¦326266 that¦326267 you all burned in¦326269 Yehudah's¦326270 cities¦326269 and on Yerushalem's¦326272 streets¦326271—you and your ancestors¦326274, your kings¦326275 and leaders, and the people¦326277 of¦326277 the land¦326278, and didn't¦326263 it¦326282 come¦326282 \add back\add* to his¦326285 \add ≈mind¦326285\add*?
\v 22 \add ≈Eventually¦326290,\add* he¦326289 could no longer bear it because of your wicked¦326294 \add ≈behaviour\add*, \add i.e.,\add* because of the¦326297 detestable \add <things\add* that¦326298 you all did¦326299. Then¦326287 your land¦326301 became¦326300 a \add ≈deserted wasteland¦326303\add* and¦326287 a curse¦326304, without inhabitants¦326306 as it is today.
